window.QI18N={"(alif) to": "(alif) zuwa", "(yaa). No new letters today. This lesson tests": "(yaa). Babu sabon harafi yau. Wannan darasi yana gwada", "(yaa). This lesson covers the": "(yaa). Wannan darasi ya ƙunshi", "(yaa). You know ا – ض. This lesson adds": "(yaa). Ka san ا – ض. Wannan darasi yana ƙara", "(yaa). You know ا – ك. This lesson adds the": "(yaa). Ka san ا – ك. Wannan darasi yana ƙara", ") is a small slanted stroke": ") ƙaramin layi ne mai karkata", ", and then you know the whole alphabet:": ", sannan ka san dukan baƙaƙe:", ", from": ", daga", "A boat shape with ONE dot below.": "Siffar jirgin ruwa mai ɗigo ƊAYA a ƙasa.", "A breathy h from the middle of the throat (no English equivalent). Not the light h of “hat”.": "H mai iska daga tsakiyar maƙogwaro. Ba ita ce h mai sauƙi ba.", "A curve with ONE dot inside.": "Lanƙwasa mai ɗigo ƊAYA a ciki.", "A curved shape with TWO dots below.": "Siffa mai lanƙwasa, ɗigo BIYU a ƙasa.", "A deep q from the very back of the mouth. Never “k” and never a glottal stop.": "Q mai zurfi daga can ƙarshen baki. Ba \"k\" ba ce, ba kuma hamza ba.", "A dot above. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo ɗaya a sama. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "A dot inside. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo ɗaya a ciki. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "A heavy d made with the side of the tongue against the upper back teeth. Arabic is called “the language of ḍaad” because of this sound.": "D mai nauyi da ake furtawa da gefen harshe a kan haƙoran sama na baya. Ana kiran Larabci \"harshen ḍaad\" saboda wannan sauti.", "A heavy t: press the tongue tip up and raise the back of the tongue, mouth full. Not the light ت.": "T mai nauyi: ɗaga kan harshe sama ka ɗaga bayan harshe, baki a cike. Ba ت mai sauƙi ba.", "A heavy “th” as in “this”, tongue between the teeth, mouth full. Never “z”.": "\"Dh\" mai nauyi, harshe tsakanin haƙora, baki a cike. Kada ka faɗi \"z\".", "A heavy, full s: lift the back of the tongue and round the mouth. Not the light س.": "S mai nauyi kuma cikakke: ɗaga bayan harshe ka zagaye baki. Ba س mai sauƙi ba.", "A letter can have a shadda and a tanween together: sabbun, haqqan. Double the letter, then add the n sound.": "Harafi zai iya samun shadda da tanwin tare: sabbun, haqqan. Ninka harafin, sannan ka ƙara sautin n.", "A letter changes its shape at the start, middle and end of a word, but its sound stays the same.": "Siffar harafi tana canzawa a farko, tsakiya da ƙarshen kalma, amma sautinsa ba ya canzawa.", "A letter changes its shape at the start, the middle and the end of a word, but its sound stays the same. You will also learn the seven heavy letters.": "Siffar harafi tana canzawa a farko, tsakiya da ƙarshen kalma, amma sautinsa ba ya canzawa. Za ka kuma koyi baƙaƙe bakwai masu nauyi.", "A light h as in “hat”, from the bottom of the throat. Different from the breathy ح.": "H mai sauƙi daga ƙasan maƙogwaro. Ta bambanta da ح mai iska.", "A loop with a deep round bowl, TWO dots above.": "Zagaye mai kwano mai zurfi, ɗigo BIYU a sama.", "A loop with a dot. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Zagaye mai ɗigo. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "A loop with a small tooth. No dot.": "Zagaye mai ƙaramin haƙori. Babu ɗigo.", "A loop with a tall upright stroke. No dot.": "Zagaye mai dogon layi a tsaye. Babu ɗigo.", "A loop, no dot. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Zagaye, babu ɗigo. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "A review of everything so far: madd, noon sakinah, tanween and meem sakinah, in Qur'anic verses.": "Bitar duk abin da aka koya: madda, nun sakina, tanwin da mim sakina, a cikin ayoyin Alƙur'ani.", "A review of shadda in longer Qur'anic phrases. Take a breath and read smoothly.": "Bitar shadda a cikin dogayen jimlolin Alƙur'ani. Ja numfashi ka karanta a hankali.", "A round bowl with ONE dot above (deeper than ب).": "Kwano zagaye mai ɗigo ƊAYA a sama (ya fi ب zurfi).", "A small bent shape. No dot.": "Ƙaramar siffa mai lanƙwasa. Babu ɗigo.", "A small curve that dips below the line. No dot.": "Ƙaramin lanƙwasa da ke sauka ƙasa da layi. Babu ɗigo.", "A small loop on a flat line, ONE dot above.": "Ƙaramin zagaye a kan layi madaidaici, ɗigo ƊAYA a sama.", "A small round head with a tail curving down. No dot.": "Ƙaramin kai zagaye mai wutsiya da ke lanƙwasa ƙasa. Babu ɗigo.", "A small round head with a tail going down.": "Ƙaramin kai zagaye mai wutsiya da ke sauka ƙasa.", "A small round loop. No dot.": "Ƙaramin zagaye. Babu ɗigo.", "A soft gargled “gh” from the top of the throat, like the French r.": "\"Gh\" mai laushi kamar kurkure, daga saman maƙogwaro.", "A straight vertical line. No dots.": "Layi madaidaici a tsaye. Babu ɗigo.", "A tall bent shape with a small mark (hamza-like) inside.": "Doguwar siffa mai lanƙwasa da ƙaramar alama (kamar hamza) a ciki.", "A tall stroke with a hook at the bottom. No dot.": "Dogon layi mai ƙugiya a ƙasa. Babu ɗigo.", "A tapped r, the tip of the tongue flicks once (like Spanish “pero”).": "R da harshe ke bugawa sau ɗaya.", "A voiced squeeze from the middle of the throat. No English equivalent; listen carefully and copy.": "Sauti mai murya da ake matsewa daga tsakiyar maƙogwaro. Saurara da kyau ka kwaikwaya.", "Aisha & Khadija": "Aisha da Khadija", "Alif Madd: Everyday Spelling": "Maddar Alif: Rubutun Yau da Kullum", "Alif Madd: Qur'anic Words": "Maddar Alif: Kalmomin Alƙur'ani", "Alif carrying a hamza ( أ ) with a fatha. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Alif mai ɗauke da hamza ( أ ) da fatha. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Allah's Blessings": "Ni'imomin Allah", "Allah's Greatness": "Girman Allah", "Almost! Listen and try again.": "Kusan! Saurara ka sake gwadawa.", "Alphabet Review": "Bitar Baƙaƙe", "Alphabet order": "Jerin baƙaƙe", "Alphabet review": "Bitar baƙaƙe", "Alphabet review!": "Bitar baƙaƙe!", "An open curve on top, a bowl below. No dot.": "Lanƙwasa a buɗe a sama, kwano a ƙasa. Babu ɗigo.", "Arabic has": "Larabci yana da", "Assalamu alaikum! It's Nuri again. You already know seven letters, from Alif to Kha. Masha'Allah!": "Assalamu alaikum! Ni ce Nuri kuma. Ka riga ka san baƙaƙe bakwai, daga Alif zuwa Kha. Masha'Allah!", "Assalamu alaikum! It's Nuri. Masha'Allah, you know all twenty eight letters! Now we learn the fatha. The fatha is a small line on top of the letter. It makes the sound a.": "Assalamu alaikum! Ni ce Nuri. Masha'Allah, ka san dukan baƙaƙe ashirin da takwas! Yanzu za mu koyi fatha. Fatha ƙaramin layi ne a saman harafi. Sautinsa \"a\".", "Assalamu alaikum! It's Nuri. The fatha is a small line on top of the letter. It makes the sound a.": "Assalamu alaikum! Ni ce Nuri. Fatha ƙaramin layi ne a saman harafi. Sautinsa \"a\".", "Assalamu alaikum! It's Nuri. You already know fifteen letters, from Alif to Daad. Masha'Allah!": "Assalamu alaikum! Ni ce Nuri. Ka riga ka san baƙaƙe goma sha biyar, daga Alif zuwa Daad. Masha'Allah!", "Assalamu alaikum! It's Nuri. You already know twenty two letters, from Alif to Kaaf. Masha'Allah!": "Assalamu alaikum! Ni ce Nuri. Ka riga ka san baƙaƙe ashirin da biyu, daga Alif zuwa Kaaf. Masha'Allah!", "Assalamu alaikum, and welcome to the Qira'ah class. In this course you will learn to read the Qur'an correctly, step by step, with the book Nour al-Bayan.": "Assalamu alaikum, barka da zuwa ajin Qira'ah. A wannan kwas za ka koyi karanta Alƙur'ani daidai, mataki-mataki, da littafin Nour al-Bayan.", "At the start of a word يـ looks like بـ, but with TWO dots below.": "A farkon kalma يـ yana kama da بـ, amma da ɗigo BIYU a ƙasa.", "Barakallahu feekum!": "Barakallahu feekum!", "Big Final Check": "Babban Jarrabawar Ƙarshe", "Both are “h”: ه is light (hat), ح is breathy from the throat.": "Duka biyun \"h\" ne: ه mai sauƙi ce, ح mai iska ce daga maƙogwaro.", "Bubble catch!": "Kama kumfa!", "Bubble time! Tap the green button, then catch only the bubbles with this letter.": "Lokacin kumfa! Danna maɓallin kore, sannan ka kama kumfar da ke da wannan harafi kawai.", "Build": "Gina", "Build the word": "Gina kalmar", "Build what you hear.": "Gina abin da ka ji.", "Check": "Duba", "Close lesson": "Rufe darasi", "Correct — well done": "Daidai ne, madalla", "Damma": "Damma", "Damma Words": "Kalmomin Damma", "Damma Words in Two Steps": "Kalmomin Damma a Matakai Biyu", "Damma: Whole Words": "Damma: Cikakkun Kalmomi", "Dictation": "Rubutun ji", "Dots": "Ɗigo", "Each picture starts with a letter. Tap the picture, then its letter.": "Kowane hoto yana farawa da harafi. Danna hoton, sannan harafinsa.", "Exam": "Jarrabawa", "Fatha": "Fatha", "Fatha time! ـَ": "Lokacin fatha! ـَ", "Final check": "Jarrabawar ƙarshe", "Final check! Listen or look, then choose the right letter.": "Jarrabawar ƙarshe! Saurara ko duba, sannan ka zaɓi harafin da ya dace.", "Find the missing letter": "Nemo harafin da ya ɓace", "Find the missing letter, then write the letters in order from the beginning.": "Nemo harafin da ya ɓace, sannan ka rubuta baƙaƙen a jere daga farko.", "First Words": "Kalmomin Farko", "First, short and long pairs, so you hear the difference. Then Qur'anic words with the waw madd. Remember: an alif with a small round zero is silent.": "Da farko, nau'i-nau'i gajere da dogo don ka ji bambancin. Sannan kalmomin Alƙur'ani masu maddar waw. Ka tuna: alif mai ƙaramin sifiri zagaye ba a karanta shi.", "Follow the dots with your finger": "Bi ɗigogin da yatsanka", "Get them all right to win the badge": "Amsa duka daidai don ka ci lambar yabo", "Hamza in the Middle & at the End": "Hamza a Tsakiya da a Ƙarshe", "Hamzatul Wasl & the Moon Laam": "Hamzatul Wasl da Laamul Qamariyya", "Hamzatul Wasl is an alif you only pronounce when you start with it. After another word it is silent. With the moon letters, you pronounce the laam clearly: al qamar.": "Hamzatul Wasl alif ce da ake furtawa kawai idan ka fara da ita. Bayan wata kalma ba a karanta ta. Da baƙaƙen qamariyya, ana furta laam a fili: al qamar.", "Harakat Review": "Bitar Harakoki", "Heavy letter.": "Harafi mai nauyi.", "Heavy letters": "Baƙaƙe masu nauyi", "Heavy or light": "Mai nauyi ko mai sauƙi", "How is this read?": "Yaya ake karanta wannan?", "In everyday spelling, a hamza with a long a is written as one sign: آ, like آدَمُ. In the Mushaf it is written ءَا. Both are read the same: aa, two counts.": "A rubutun yau da kullum, hamza da dogon a ana rubuta su alama ɗaya: آ, kamar آدَمُ. A Mus'hafi ana rubuta ءَا. Duka ana karanta su iri ɗaya: aa, ƙidaya biyu.", "In the Mushaf, a hamza with a long a is written ءَا, like ءَادَمُ.": "A Mus'hafi, hamza da dogon a ana rubuta ءَا, kamar ءَادَمُ.", "In this lesson you read the first two letters together as one sound, then add the third letter, like sa'a, then da: sa'ada.": "A wannan darasi za ka karanta baƙaƙe biyu na farko tare a matsayin sauti ɗaya, sannan ka ƙara na uku, kamar sa'a, sannan da: sa'ada.", "In this lesson you will learn eight more letters, from Daal to Daad. Four pairs look almost the same, so we will focus on the dots that tell them apart.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi ƙarin baƙaƙe takwas, daga Daal zuwa Daad. Nau'i huɗu sun kusa kama da juna, don haka za mu mai da hankali ga ɗigogin da ke bambanta su.", "In this lesson you will learn seven more letters, from Taa to Kaaf, including two sounds from the throat, Ayn and Ghayn, and the deep Qaaf.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi ƙarin baƙaƙe bakwai, daga Taa zuwa Kaaf, har da sautuka biyu daga maƙogwaro, Ayn da Ghayn, da Qaaf mai zurfi.", "In this lesson you will learn the first seven letters of the alphabet, from Alif to Kha: their names, their sounds, and how to tell the look-alike letters apart by their dots.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi baƙaƙe bakwai na farko, daga Alif zuwa Kha: sunayensu, sautukansu, da yadda za ka bambance masu kama da juna ta ɗigogi.", "In this lesson you will learn the last six letters, from Laam to Yaa. After this, you will know the whole alphabet.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi baƙaƙe shida na ƙarshe, daga Laam zuwa Yaa. Bayan haka, za ka san dukan baƙaƙe.", "In this lesson you will read nine more letters with fatha, from Raa to Ayn, and practise the heavy letters that fill the mouth.": "A wannan darasi za ka karanta ƙarin baƙaƙe tara da fatha, daga Raa zuwa Ayn, ka kuma yi atisayen baƙaƙe masu nauyi da ke cika baki.", "In this lesson you will read the last ten letters with fatha, from Ghayn to Yaa. After this, you can read every letter with a fatha.": "A wannan darasi za ka karanta baƙaƙe goma na ƙarshe da fatha, daga Ghayn zuwa Yaa. Bayan haka, za ka iya karanta kowane harafi da fatha.", "Intro": "Gabatarwa", "Is this letter heavy or light?": "Wannan harafi mai nauyi ne ko mai sauƙi?", "Kasra": "Kasra", "Kasra Phrases": "Jimlolin Kasra", "Kasra Words": "Kalmomin Kasra", "Kasra Words in Two Steps": "Kalmomin Kasra a Matakai Biyu", "Kasra: Whole Words": "Kasra: Cikakkun Kalmomi", "Learn": "Koya", "Let's go →": "Mu tafi →", "Let's read Arabic!": "Mu karanta Larabci!", "Letter Shapes": "Siffofin Baƙaƙe", "Letter shapes": "Siffofin baƙaƙe", "Letters Read but Not Written": "Baƙaƙen da ake Karantawa amma Ba a Rubuta Su", "Listen": "Saurara", "Listen & choose": "Saurara ka zaɓa", "Listen and choose": "Saurara ka zaɓa", "Listen carefully, then pop the balloon with the right letter.": "Saurara da kyau, sannan ka fasa balan-balan mai harafin da ya dace.", "Listen to the name, then tap the mic and say it. The app checks you.": "Saurari sunan, sannan ka danna makirufo ka faɗe shi. Manhajar za ta duba ka.", "Listen, then choose the letter.": "Saurara, sannan ka zaɓi harafin.", "Listen, then choose what you hear.": "Saurara, sannan ka zaɓi abin da ka ji.", "Listen, then choose.": "Saurara, sannan ka zaɓa.", "Listen, then pop the right letter": "Saurara, sannan ka fasa harafin da ya dace", "Listen, then tap the letters in order. Use ⌫ to fix a mistake.": "Saurara, sannan ka danna baƙaƙen a jere. Yi amfani da ⌫ don gyara kuskure.", "Listen, then tap the letters in the order you hear them. Use ⌫ to fix a mistake.": "Saurara, sannan ka danna baƙaƙen yadda ka ji su a jere. Yi amfani da ⌫ don gyara kuskure.", "Listen, then tap the letters you hear": "Saurara, sannan ka danna baƙaƙen da ka ji", "Listen, then tap the mic and read it": "Saurara, sannan ka danna makirufo ka karanta", "Listen, then tap the mic and read it aloud. The app checks you.": "Saurara, sannan ka danna makirufo ka karanta da ƙarfi. Manhajar za ta duba ka.", "Listen, then tap the mic and say the letter's name": "Saurara, sannan ka danna makirufo ka faɗi sunan harafin", "Listen, then tap the one you hear.": "Saurara, sannan ka danna abin da ka ji.", "Listen, then write it.": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta.", "Listening": "Sauraro", "Longer Qur'anic phrases. Take a breath, read word by word, then read the whole phrase smoothly.": "Dogayen jimlolin Alƙur'ani. Ja numfashi, karanta kalma-kalma, sannan ka karanta jimlar gaba ɗaya a hankali.", "Longer Qur'anic words with sukun. Remember: an alif with a small round zero is silent.": "Dogayen kalmomin Alƙur'ani masu sukun. Ka tuna: alif mai ƙaramin sifiri zagaye ba a karanta shi.", "Look at the shape, then choose the letter it belongs to.": "Duba siffar, sannan ka zaɓi harafin da take nasa.", "Look-alike Letters": "Baƙaƙe Masu Kama da Juna", "Look-alike letters": "Baƙaƙe masu kama da juna", "Look-alikes": "Masu kama", "Loop on top: ف one dot, ق two dots and a deeper bowl.": "Zagaye a sama: ف ɗigo ɗaya, ق ɗigo biyu da kwano mai zurfi.", "Madd Practice": "Atisayen Madda", "Madd with Alif": "Madda da Alif", "Madd with Waw": "Madda da Waw", "Madd with Yaa": "Madda da Yaa", "Madd with alif. When a letter with fatha is followed by an alif, the a sound is stretched to two counts. Listen: short, then long.": "Madda da alif. Idan harafi mai fatha alif ta biyo shi, ana jan sautin a ƙidaya biyu. Saurara: gajere, sannan dogo.", "Madd with waw. A letter with damma followed by a waw is stretched to two counts. Listen: short, then long.": "Madda da waw. Harafi mai damma da waw ta biyo shi ana jan shi ƙidaya biyu. Saurara: gajere, sannan dogo.", "Madd with yaa. A letter with kasra followed by a yaa is stretched to two counts. Listen: short, then long.": "Madda da yaa. Harafi mai kasra da yaa ta biyo shi ana jan shi ƙidaya biyu. Saurara: gajere, sannan dogo.", "Many letters share a shape. The dots tell them apart.": "Baƙaƙe da yawa suna da siffa ɗaya. Ɗigogi ne ke bambanta su.", "Masha'Allah!": "Masha'Allah!", "Masha'Allah! Now it is your turn to read and play!": "Masha'Allah! Yanzu lokacinka ne ka karanta ka yi wasa!", "Masha'Allah! Now you know fifteen letters, from Alif to Daad! You earned the Letter Explorer badge.": "Masha'Allah! Yanzu ka san baƙaƙe goma sha biyar, daga Alif zuwa Daad! Ka ci lambar Mai Binciken Baƙaƙe.", "Masha'Allah! Now you know twenty two letters, from Alif to Kaaf! You earned the Letter Explorer badge.": "Masha'Allah! Yanzu ka san baƙaƙe ashirin da biyu, daga Alif zuwa Kaaf! Ka ci lambar Mai Binciken Baƙaƙe.", "Masha'Allah! You are an Alphabet Champion! Next, we start reading with fatha.": "Masha'Allah! Kai Gwarzon Baƙaƙe ne! Na gaba, za mu fara karatu da fatha.", "Masha'Allah! You know Alif to Kha! You earned the Letter Explorer badge.": "Masha'Allah! Ka san Alif zuwa Kha! Ka ci lambar Mai Binciken Baƙaƙe.", "Masha'Allah! You know all twenty eight letters, from Alif to Yaa! You earned the Alphabet Champion badge.": "Masha'Allah! Ka san dukan baƙaƙe ashirin da takwas, daga Alif zuwa Yaa! Ka ci lambar Gwarzon Baƙaƙe.", "Masha'Allah! You met eight new letters. Now it is your turn to play!": "Masha'Allah! Ka haɗu da sababbin baƙaƙe takwas. Yanzu lokacinka ne ka yi wasa!", "Masha'Allah! You met seven letters. Now it is your turn to play!": "Masha'Allah! Ka haɗu da baƙaƙe bakwai. Yanzu lokacinka ne ka yi wasa!", "Masha'Allah! You met seven new letters. Now it is your turn to play!": "Masha'Allah! Ka haɗu da sababbin baƙaƙe bakwai. Yanzu lokacinka ne ka yi wasa!", "Masha'Allah! You met the last six letters. Now it is your turn to play!": "Masha'Allah! Ka haɗu da baƙaƙe shida na ƙarshe. Yanzu lokacinka ne ka yi wasa!", "Match": "Haɗa", "Match each letter to its name": "Haɗa kowane harafi da sunansa", "Match the picture": "Haɗa hoton", "Meem Sakinah & Ghunnah": "Mim Sakina da Gunna", "Meet the letters": "Haɗu da baƙaƙe", "More Qur'anic phrases with every kind of madd. Take care with the silent alif and the small letters.": "Ƙarin jimlolin Alƙur'ani da kowane irin madda. Kula da alif da ba a karantawa da ƙananan baƙaƙe.", "More Qur'anic phrases with shadda. Read word by word, then the whole phrase.": "Ƙarin jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu shadda. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya.", "More Tajweed Rules": "Ƙarin Dokokin Tajwidi", "More Words": "Ƙarin Kalmomi", "More about the hamza: in the middle and at the end of a word, its seat follows the vowel before it.": "Ƙari game da hamza: a tsakiya da ƙarshen kalma, kujerarta tana bin wasalin da ke gabanta.", "More letters": "Ƙarin baƙaƙe", "More phrases with sukun. Listen for the qalqalah letters, qaf, taa, baa, jeem and daal: with a sukun they bounce slightly.": "Ƙarin jimloli masu sukun. Saurari baƙaƙen qalqala, qaf, taa, baa, jim da daal: idan suna da sukun suna ɗan yin amo.", "More review phrases. Notice the silent alif in mi-ah: an alif with a small round zero is never read.": "Ƙarin jimlolin bita. Lura da alif da ba a karantawa a mi-ah: alif mai ƙaramin sifiri zagaye ba a taɓa karanta shi.", "More review practice. Take your time: madd, ghunnah, merging and qalqalah.": "Ƙarin atisayen bita. A hankali: madda, gunna, idgami da qalqala.", "More three letter words with fatha. Read each letter, then read the whole word without stopping.": "Ƙarin kalmomi masu baƙaƙe uku da fatha. Karanta kowane harafi, sannan ka karanta kalmar gaba ɗaya ba tare da tsayawa ba.", "More verses and hadith. Read slowly and beautifully.": "Ƙarin ayoyi da hadisai. Karanta a hankali kuma da kyau.", "Mumtaz! Excellent!": "Mumtaz! Madalla sosai!", "Name": "Suna", "Next letter →": "Harafi na gaba →", "Next →": "Gaba →", "Next ▶": "Gaba ▶", "No dot, dips below the line. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Babu ɗigo, yana sauka ƙasa da layi. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "No dot. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Babu ɗigo. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "No new letters today. This lesson tests": "Babu sabon harafi yau. Wannan darasi yana gwada", "No sound of its own: it carries a hamza (a short catch, as in “uh‑oh”) or stretches a vowel into “aa”.": "Ba shi da sautin kansa: yana ɗaukar hamza (ɗan tsayawa) ko yana jan wasali ya zama \"aa\".", "Noon Sakinah Practice": "Atisayen Nun Sakina", "Nour al-Bayan ·": "Nour al-Bayan ·", "Now read each word in one go, without splitting it. Some words are longer. Take your time.": "Yanzu karanta kowace kalma a lokaci ɗaya, ba tare da raba ta ba. Wasu kalmomi sun fi tsawo. A hankali.", "Now read each word in one go, without splitting it. Take care with the letters that sound alike.": "Yanzu karanta kowace kalma a lokaci ɗaya, ba tare da raba ta ba. Kula da baƙaƙen da sautinsu ya yi kama.", "Now the rules of noon sakinah and tanween. Before the throat letters the noon is clear. Before ya, noon, meem and waw it merges with a nasal sound. Before laam and raa it disappears.": "Yanzu dokokin nun sakina da tanwin. Kafin baƙaƙen maƙogwaro, nun tana bayyana. Kafin ya, nun, mim da waw tana haɗewa da sautin hanci. Kafin laam da raa tana ɓacewa.", "Now trace the letter with your finger. Follow the dots.": "Yanzu zana harafin da yatsanka. Bi ɗigogin.", "Now we start reading. In this lesson you will meet the fatha, a small stroke above a letter that adds a short a sound, and read the first nine letters with it, from Alif to Dhaal.": "Yanzu za mu fara karatu. A wannan darasi za ka haɗu da fatha, ƙaramin layi a saman harafi da ke ƙara gajeren sautin a, ka karanta baƙaƙe tara na farko da ita, daga Alif zuwa Dhaal.", "Now write all the letters in order, from Alif to Kha. Start with Alif!": "Yanzu ka rubuta dukan baƙaƙe a jere, daga Alif zuwa Kha. Fara da Alif!", "Now write all the letters you know, in order. Start with Alif, and go all the way to Daad!": "Yanzu ka rubuta dukan baƙaƙen da ka sani a jere. Fara da Alif, har zuwa Daad!", "Now write all the letters you know, in order. Start with Alif, and go all the way to Kaaf!": "Yanzu ka rubuta dukan baƙaƙen da ka sani a jere. Fara da Alif, har zuwa Kaaf!", "Now write the whole alphabet, in order, from Alif to Yaa. You can do it!": "Yanzu ka rubuta dukan baƙaƙe a jere, daga Alif zuwa Yaa. Za ka iya!", "Now write them in order with the fatha. Start with Alif!": "Yanzu ka rubuta su a jere da fatha. Fara da Alif!", "Now you compare the spelling of the Mushaf with everyday spelling. The sounds are the same; only the marks are different.": "Yanzu za ka kwatanta rubutun Mus'hafi da rubutun yau da kullum. Sautukan iri ɗaya ne; alamomi ne kawai suka bambanta.", "Now you learn the shadda: a small sign like a W above a letter. It doubles the letter, so you press on it: bad, da, becomes badda.": "Yanzu za ka koyi shadda: ƙaramar alama kamar W a saman harafi. Tana ninka harafin, don haka ka matsa a kai: bad, da, ya zama badda.", "Now you meet Hamzatul Wasl, the alif you only say when you start with it, and the moon laam, a laam with sukun that you pronounce clearly.": "Yanzu za ka haɗu da Hamzatul Wasl, alif da kake furtawa kawai idan ka fara da ita, da laamul qamariyya, laam mai sukun da kake furtawa a fili.", "Now you meet the small alif, a little vertical stroke above a letter. You find it only in the Qur'an, and it is read as a long a, two counts.": "Yanzu za ka haɗu da ƙaramar alif, ƙaramin layi a tsaye a saman harafi. Ana samun ta a cikin Alƙur'ani kawai, kuma ana karanta ta dogon a, ƙidaya biyu.", "Now you read phrases with fatha and kasra. Read word by word, then the whole phrase in one breath.": "Yanzu za ka karanta jimloli masu fatha da kasra. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya a numfashi ɗaya.", "Now you read real words! Each word has three letters with fatha. Read each letter, then join them into one word, like ra, ka, a: raka'a.": "Yanzu za ka karanta kalmomi na gaske! Kowace kalma tana da baƙaƙe uku masu fatha. Karanta kowane harafi, sannan ka haɗa su kalma ɗaya, kamar ra, ka, a: raka'a.", "Now you read short phrases. Read the first word, then the second, then read them together in one breath, like raka'a wa sajada.": "Yanzu za ka karanta gajerun jimloli. Karanta kalma ta farko, sannan ta biyu, sannan ka karanta su tare a numfashi ɗaya, kamar raka'a wa sajada.", "Now you read words with fatha and kasra. Read each letter, then join them, like ra, ki, ba: rakiba.": "Yanzu za ka karanta kalmomi masu fatha da kasra. Karanta kowane harafi, sannan ka haɗa su, kamar ra, ki, ba: rakiba.", "One dot above, round bowl. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo ɗaya a sama, kwano zagaye. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "One dot above. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo ɗaya a sama. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "One dot below. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo ɗaya a ƙasa. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Open curve with a dot. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Lanƙwasa a buɗe mai ɗigo. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Open curve, no dot. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Lanƙwasa a buɗe, babu ɗigo. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Order": "Jeri", "Pause": "Dakata", "Pop the balloon!": "Fasa balan-balan!", "Practice the noon sakinah and tanween rules in Qur'anic verses. In each one, find the noon or tanween, and the letter after it.": "Yi atisayen dokokin nun sakina da tanwin a cikin ayoyin Alƙur'ani. A kowace aya, nemo nun ko tanwin, da harafin da ke bayansa.", "Practice time. In each verse, find every madd: is it two counts, four to five, or six? Listen, then read after the teacher.": "Lokacin atisaye. A kowace aya, nemo kowace madda: ƙidaya biyu ce, huɗu zuwa biyar, ko shida? Saurara, sannan ka karanta bayan malami.", "Preparatory": "Share Fage", "Preparatory Final Exam": "Jarrabawar Ƙarshe ta Share Fage", "Qira'ah": "Qira'ah", "Qur'anic and everyday spelling": "Rubutun Alƙur'ani da na yau da kullum", "Qur'anic phrases": "Jimlolin Alƙur'ani", "Qur'anic phrases with every kind of shadda. Read word by word, then the whole phrase.": "Jimlolin Alƙur'ani da kowane irin shadda. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya.", "Qur'anic phrases with shadda and the sun laam. Remember: Hamzatul Wasl in the middle of a phrase is silent.": "Jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu shadda da laamush shamsiyya. Ka tuna: Hamzatul Wasl a tsakiyar jimla ba a karanta ta.", "Qur'anic phrases with sukun. Read word by word, then the whole phrase.": "Jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu sukun. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya.", "Qur'anic phrases with tanween fath. Read the whole phrase smoothly.": "Jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu tanwin fath. Karanta jimlar gaba ɗaya a hankali.", "Qur'anic phrases with tanween. Read the phrase smoothly, in one breath.": "Jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu tanwin. Karanta jimlar a hankali, a numfashi ɗaya.", "Qur'anic verses": "Ayoyin Alƙur'ani", "Qur'anic vs Everyday Spelling": "Rubutun Alƙur'ani da Rubutun Yau da Kullum", "Qur'anic words": "Kalmomin Alƙur'ani", "Qur'anic words and phrases ending in tanween fath. Say the an clearly, and don't stretch the alif after it.": "Kalmomi da jimlolin Alƙur'ani da ke ƙarewa da tanwin fath. Faɗi \"an\" a fili, kada ka ja alif da ke bayansa.", "Qur'anic words and phrases with shadda and kasra. Press on the doubled letter.": "Kalmomi da jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu shadda da kasra. Matsa a kan harafin da aka ninka.", "Qur'anic words and phrases with tanween kasr and tanween fath. Look carefully at the last letter of each word.": "Kalmomi da jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu tanwin kasr da tanwin fath. Duba harafin ƙarshe na kowace kalma da kyau.", "Qur'anic words with shadda and damma. Listen to each one carefully before you read.": "Kalmomin Alƙur'ani masu shadda da damma. Saurari kowace da kyau kafin ka karanta.", "Qur'anic words with shadda. Press on the doubled letter, and keep any madd after it for two counts.": "Kalmomin Alƙur'ani masu shadda. Matsa a kan harafin da aka ninka, ka kuma riƙe duk maddar da ke bayansa ƙidaya biyu.", "Qur'anic words with sukun. Read the open syllable, then the closed one, then the whole word.": "Kalmomin Alƙur'ani masu sukun. Karanta gaɓar a buɗe, sannan ta rufe, sannan kalmar gaba ɗaya.", "Qur'anic words with the yaa madd. Make every long ii exactly two counts, and keep the short vowels short.": "Kalmomin Alƙur'ani masu maddar yaa. Sa kowane dogon ii ya zama ƙidaya biyu daidai, ka bar gajerun wasula gajeru.", "Read & repeat": "Karanta ka maimaita", "Read each word in one go. Many words now have four or five letters. Look at every harakah.": "Karanta kowace kalma a lokaci ɗaya. Yanzu kalmomi da yawa suna da baƙaƙe huɗu ko biyar. Duba kowace haraka.", "Read it, then tap the mic": "Karanta, sannan ka danna makirufo", "Read the first two letters together as one sound, then add the third, like daḥi, then ka: daḥika.": "Karanta baƙaƙe biyu na farko tare a matsayin sauti ɗaya, sannan ka ƙara na uku, kamar daḥi, sannan ka: daḥika.", "Read the first two letters together, then add the third, like busi, then ṭa: busiṭa. Then read whole words.": "Karanta baƙaƙe biyu na farko tare, sannan ka ƙara na uku, kamar busi, sannan ṭa: busiṭa. Sannan ka karanta cikakkun kalmomi.", "Read the word aloud, then tap the mic. The app checks you.": "Karanta kalmar da ƙarfi, sannan ka danna makirufo. Manhajar za ta duba ka.", "Reading": "Karatu", "Reads": "Ana karanta", "Recognise": "Gane", "Replay": "Sake kunnawa", "Review practice. Read each verse slowly, applying every tajweed rule you have learned.": "Atisayen bita. Karanta kowace aya a hankali, kana amfani da duk dokokin tajwidi da ka koya.", "Review time! These phrases mix fatha, kasra and damma. Read word by word, then the whole phrase.": "Lokacin bita! Waɗannan jimloli sun haɗa fatha, kasra da damma. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya.", "Review time. These Qur'anic phrases mix every madd you learned: big and small alif, yaa and waw. Read word by word, then the whole phrase.": "Lokacin bita. Waɗannan jimlolin Alƙur'ani sun haɗa kowace madda da ka koya: babbar alif da ƙarama, yaa da waw. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya.", "Review: Everyday Spelling": "Bita: Rubutun Yau da Kullum", "Review: Qur'anic verses with tajweed, then hadith in everyday spelling. Remember, everyday spelling is read without the tajweed marks.": "Bita: ayoyin Alƙur'ani da tajwidi, sannan hadisai a rubutun yau da kullum. Ka tuna, rubutun yau da kullum ana karanta shi ba tare da alamomin tajwidi ba.", "Round head with a tail. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Kai zagaye mai wutsiya. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Same boat, THREE dots above.": "Jirgin ruwa iri ɗaya, ɗigo UKU a sama.", "Same boat, TWO dots above.": "Jirgin ruwa iri ɗaya, ɗigo BIYU a sama.", "Same curve as ر, ONE dot above.": "Lanƙwasa iri ɗaya da ر, ɗigo ƊAYA a sama.", "Same curve, NO dot.": "Lanƙwasa iri ɗaya, BABU ɗigo.", "Same curve, ONE dot above.": "Lanƙwasa iri ɗaya, ɗigo ƊAYA a sama.", "Same loop as ص, ONE dot above.": "Zagaye iri ɗaya da ص, ɗigo ƊAYA a sama.", "Same loop: no dot, dot above.": "Zagaye iri ɗaya: babu ɗigo, ɗigo a sama.", "Same shape as د, ONE dot above.": "Siffa iri ɗaya da د, ɗigo ƊAYA a sama.", "Same shape as ط, ONE dot above.": "Siffa iri ɗaya da ط, ɗigo ƊAYA a sama.", "Same shape as ع, ONE dot above.": "Siffa iri ɗaya da ع, ɗigo ƊAYA a sama.", "Same shape — dot inside, no dot, dot above.": "Siffa iri ɗaya: ɗigo a ciki, babu ɗigo, ɗigo a sama.", "Same shape: no dot, dot above.": "Siffa iri ɗaya: babu ɗigo, ɗigo a sama.", "Same three teeth, THREE dots above.": "Haƙora uku iri ɗaya, ɗigo UKU a sama.", "Sami & Yusuf": "Sami da Yusuf", "Seven letters are always heavy (the mouth is full): خ ص ض غ ط ق ظ. Is the letter heavy or light?": "Baƙaƙe bakwai kullum masu nauyi ne (baki yana cika): خ ص ض غ ط ق ظ. Harafin mai nauyi ne ko mai sauƙi?", "Shadda Review": "Bitar Shadda", "Shadda means the letter is doubled. The first one has a sukun, the second one has the damma. Listen: single, then doubled.": "Shadda tana nufin an ninka harafin. Na farko yana da sukun, na biyu yana da damma. Saurara: guda ɗaya, sannan ninki.", "Shadda means the letter is doubled. The first one has a sukun, the second one has the fatha. Listen: single, then doubled.": "Shadda tana nufin an ninka harafin. Na farko yana da sukun, na biyu yana da fatha. Saurara: guda ɗaya, sannan ninki.", "Shadda means the letter is doubled. The first one has a sukun, the second one has the kasra. Listen: single, then doubled.": "Shadda tana nufin an ninka harafin. Na farko yana da sukun, na biyu yana da kasra. Saurara: guda ɗaya, sannan ninki.", "Shadda with Damma": "Shadda da Damma", "Shadda with Damma: Words": "Shadda da Damma: Kalmomi", "Shadda with Fatha": "Shadda da Fatha", "Shadda with Kasra": "Shadda da Kasra", "Shadda with Kasra: Words": "Shadda da Kasra: Kalmomi", "Shadda with Tanween": "Shadda da Tanwin", "Shadda with Tanween: Phrases": "Shadda da Tanwin: Jimloli", "Shadda with damma: af, fu, becomes affu. Then you read pairs like sabba and yasubbu.": "Shadda da damma: af, fu, ya zama affu. Sannan za ka karanta nau'i-nau'i kamar sabba da yasubbu.", "Shadda with kasra: rab, bi, becomes rabbi. In the Mushaf the kasra sits under the letter; in everyday spelling it can sit under the shadda.": "Shadda da kasra: rab, bi, ya zama rabbi. A Mus'hafi kasra tana ƙarƙashin harafi; a rubutun yau da kullum tana iya kasancewa ƙarƙashin shadda.", "Shadda: Qur'anic Words": "Shadda: Kalmomin Alƙur'ani", "Shapes": "Siffofi", "Short Phrases": "Gajerun Jimloli", "Short sentences in everyday spelling. Read word by word, then the whole sentence.": "Gajerun jimloli a rubutun yau da kullum. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya.", "Similar Letters Meeting": "Haɗuwar Baƙaƙe Masu Kama", "Similar bowls: ن one dot above (deeper), ب one below, ت two above.": "Kwanoni masu kama: ن ɗigo ɗaya a sama (mai zurfi), ب ɗaya a ƙasa, ت biyu a sama.", "Skip": "Tsallake", "Small round head. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ƙaramin kai zagaye. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Small round loop. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ƙaramin zagaye. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Some letters are hiding! Find the missing letter.": "Wasu baƙaƙe suna ɓoye! Nemo harafin da ya ɓace.", "Some letters look alike, and some sound alike. Today you will train your eyes and your ears to tell them apart.": "Wasu baƙaƙe sun yi kama a siffa, wasu kuma a sauti. Yau za ka horar da idanunka da kunnuwanka don bambance su.", "Some more rules: qalqalah, when raa is heavy or light, the silent letters, and how to start with Hamzatul Wasl.": "Wasu ƙarin dokoki: qalqala, lokacin da raa ke da nauyi ko sauƙi, baƙaƙen da ba a karantawa, da yadda ake farawa da Hamzatul Wasl.", "Some words have a long a that you read but do not write, like haadhaa and dhaalika. The Mushaf shows it with a small alif; normal books show nothing.": "Wasu kalmomi suna da dogon a da ake karantawa amma ba a rubuta shi, kamar haadhaa da dhaalika. Mus'hafi yana nuna shi da ƙaramar alif; littattafai na yau da kullum ba sa nuna komai.", "Sound": "Sauti", "Spell & read": "Rarraba ka karanta", "Spot the dots": "Gano ɗigogi", "Start exam": "Fara jarrabawa", "Start lesson": "Fara darasi", "Start the lesson →": "Fara darasi →", "Start ▶": "Fara ▶", "Sukun": "Sukun", "Sukun in everyday spelling: a small round circle. The alif of al has no mark.": "Sukun a rubutun yau da kullum: ƙaramin da'ira. Alif na \"al\" ba ta da alama.", "Sukun means no vowel. The letter is closed and joined to the letter before it. Listen to the difference.": "Sukun tana nufin babu wasali. Harafin a rufe yake kuma yana haɗe da harafin da ke gabansa. Saurari bambancin.", "Sukun: Everyday Spelling": "Sukun: Rubutun Yau da Kullum", "Sukun: Words & Phrases": "Sukun: Kalmomi da Jimloli", "Tajweed Review": "Bitar Tajwidi", "Take your time, and listen carefully. Bismillah, let's begin.": "A hankali, ka saurara da kyau. Bismillah, mu fara.", "Tall bent shape. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Doguwar siffa mai lanƙwasa. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Tall stroke with a hook. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Dogon layi mai ƙugiya. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Tanween Damm": "Tanwin Damm", "Tanween Damm: Words": "Tanwin Damm: Kalmomi", "Tanween Fath": "Tanwin Fath", "Tanween Fath: Phrases": "Tanwin Fath: Jimloli", "Tanween Fath: Words": "Tanwin Fath: Kalmomi", "Tanween Kasr": "Tanwin Kasr", "Tanween Kasr: Phrases": "Tanwin Kasr: Jimloli", "Tanween Kasr: Words": "Tanwin Kasr: Kalmomi", "Tanween damm is a double damma above the last letter. It sounds like un: bu becomes bun.": "Tanwin damm damma biyu ne a saman harafin ƙarshe. Sautinsa \"un\": bu ya zama bun.", "Tanween damm is a double damma. It sounds like un: bun.": "Tanwin damm damma biyu ne. Sautinsa \"un\": bun.", "Tanween fath is a double fatha. It sounds like an: ban. An alif usually follows it, but that alif is not stretched.": "Tanwin fath fatha biyu ne. Sautinsa \"an\": ban. Yawanci alif tana biye da shi, amma ba a jan wannan alif.", "Tanween is a doubled harakah at the end of a word. Tanween fath is a double fatha and sounds like an: ba becomes ban.": "Tanwin haraka ce da aka ninka a ƙarshen kalma. Tanwin fath fatha biyu ne kuma sautinsa \"an\": ba ya zama ban.", "Tanween kasr is a double kasra under the last letter. It sounds like in: bi becomes bin.": "Tanwin kasr kasra biyu ne a ƙarƙashin harafin ƙarshe. Sautinsa \"in\": bi ya zama bin.", "Tanween kasr is a double kasra under the letter. It sounds like in: bin.": "Tanwin kasr kasra biyu ne a ƙarƙashin harafi. Sautinsa \"in\": bin.", "Tap ALL the letters, from Alif to Yaa": "Danna DUKAN baƙaƙe, daga Alif zuwa Yaa", "Tap a letter, then its mark.": "Danna harafi, sannan harakarsa.", "Tap a letter, then its name.": "Danna harafi, sannan sunansa.", "Tap a picture, then tap the letter it starts with.": "Danna hoto, sannan harafin da yake farawa da shi.", "Tap and speak": "Danna ka yi magana", "Tap each letter. Hear how it is read with fatha, and how to recognise it.": "Danna kowane harafi. Ji yadda ake karanta shi da fatha, da yadda za ka gane shi.", "Tap each letter. Learn its name, its sound and how to recognise it.": "Danna kowane harafi. Koyi sunansa, sautinsa da yadda za ka gane shi.", "Tap only": "Danna kawai", "Tap the letters from Alif to Daad": "Danna baƙaƙe daga Alif zuwa Daad", "Tap the letters from Alif to Kaaf": "Danna baƙaƙe daga Alif zuwa Kaaf", "Tap the letters from Alif to Kha": "Danna baƙaƙe daga Alif zuwa Kha", "Tap the mic and say the name": "Danna makirufo ka faɗi sunan", "Tap the pieces in order. Arabic is read right to left.": "Danna guntayen a jere. Ana karanta Larabci daga dama zuwa hagu.", "Tap them in order, from أَ to ذَ": "Danna su a jere, daga أَ zuwa ذَ", "Tap them in order, from أَ to عَ": "Danna su a jere, daga أَ zuwa عَ", "Tap them in order, from أَ to يَ": "Danna su a jere, daga أَ zuwa يَ", "Tap ▶ Spell: each letter is read, then the whole word. Read along with it.": "Danna ▶ Rarraba: ana karanta kowane harafi, sannan kalmar gaba ɗaya. Karanta tare da shi.", "The": "Al", "The Adhan": "Kiran Sallah", "The Alphabet": "Baƙaƙe", "The Creation of Man": "Halittar Mutum", "The Day of Eid": "Ranar Sallah", "The Farmer": "Manomi", "The Muslim": "Musulmi", "The Qur'an": "Alƙur'ani", "The Small Alif": "Ƙaramar Alif", "The Small Waw": "Ƙaramar Waw", "The Small Yaa": "Ƙaramar Yaa", "The Sparrow": "Gwara", "The Stars": "Taurari", "The Sun Laam": "Laamush Shamsiyya", "The choices differ by one letter or one harakah. Listen carefully.": "Zaɓuɓɓukan sun bambanta da harafi ɗaya ko haraka ɗaya. Saurara da kyau.", "The damma is a small waw above a letter. It adds a short u sound. Ba with damma is bu. Round your lips, and keep it short.": "Damma ƙaramar waw ce a saman harafi. Tana ƙara gajeren sautin u. Ba da damma ita ce bu. Zagaye leɓunanka, ka sa ta gajera.", "The hamza sits on alif, on waw, on yaa, or alone: أَ ؤَ ئَ ءَ — always read “a”.": "Hamza tana zama a kan alif, a kan waw, a kan yaa, ko ita kaɗai: أَ ؤَ ئَ ءَ, kullum ana karanta \"a\".", "The kasra is a small stroke under a letter. It adds a short i sound. Ba with kasra is bi. Keep the sound short and lower your lips.": "Kasra ƙaramin layi ne a ƙarƙashin harafi. Tana ƙara gajeren sautin i. Ba da kasra ita ce bi. Ka sa sautin gajere ka saukar da leɓunanka.", "The last lesson of Beginner Three: Qur'anic phrases with shadda and tanween.": "Darasi na ƙarshe na Mafari 3: jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu shadda da tanwin.", "The last lesson of the book: The Creation of Man, from Surah Al-Hajj, and a passage about the stars. Listen to each line, read it after the teacher, then read it alone.": "Darasi na ƙarshe na littafin: Halittar Mutum, daga Suratul Hajj, da wani sashe game da taurari. Saurari kowane layi, karanta shi bayan malami, sannan ka karanta shi kai kaɗai.", "The last lesson of this level: Qur'anic phrases with shadda and tanween.": "Darasi na ƙarshe na wannan mataki: jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu shadda da tanwin.", "The last letters": "Baƙaƙen ƙarshe", "The last set of Qur'anic sukun phrases. Watch the silent alifs and the Hamzatul Wasl inside the phrase.": "Rukuni na ƙarshe na jimlolin Alƙur'ani masu sukun. Kula da alif da ba a karantawa da Hamzatul Wasl a cikin jimla.", "The rules of meem sakinah: hidden before baa, merged before meem, and clear before every other letter. Noon and meem with shadda always get a nasal sound of two counts.": "Dokokin mim sakina: ɓoyayya kafin baa, haɗewa kafin mim, kuma a bayyane kafin sauran baƙaƙe. Nun da mim masu shadda kullum suna da sautin hanci na ƙidaya biyu.", "The second madd letter is yaa. A kasra followed by a yaa makes a long ii, for two counts: bi becomes bii.": "Harafin madda na biyu shi ne yaa. Kasra da yaa ta biyo ta tana yin dogon ii, ƙidaya biyu: bi ya zama bii.", "The small waw is a little waw written after a damma, mostly after the letter haa. It appears only in the Qur'an, and it is read as a long uu, two counts.": "Ƙaramar waw ƙaramar waw ce da ake rubutawa bayan damma, galibi bayan harafin haa. Tana cikin Alƙur'ani kawai, kuma ana karanta ta dogon uu, ƙidaya biyu.", "The small yaa is a little yaa written after a kasra, mostly after the letter haa. It appears only in the Qur'an, and it is read as a long ii, two counts.": "Ƙaramar yaa ƙaramar yaa ce da ake rubutawa bayan kasra, galibi bayan harafin haa. Tana cikin Alƙur'ani kawai, kuma ana karanta ta dogon ii, ƙidaya biyu.", "The third madd letter is waw. A damma followed by a waw makes a long uu, for two counts. Then we read all three madd letters together.": "Harafin madda na uku shi ne waw. Damma da waw ta biyo ta tana yin dogon uu, ƙidaya biyu. Sannan za mu karanta baƙaƙen madda uku tare.", "These pairs look or sound alike. Tap each one to hear the difference.": "Waɗannan nau'i-nau'i sun yi kama a siffa ko sauti. Danna kowane don ka ji bambancin.", "These words come from the Qur'an. Find the alif after each fatha and give it two counts, no more and no less.": "Waɗannan kalmomi daga Alƙur'ani suke. Nemo alif bayan kowace fatha ka ba ta ƙidaya biyu, ba fiye ba ba ƙasa ba.", "This is a fatha ـَ  It says “a”!": "Wannan fatha ce ـَ  Sautinta \"a\"!", "This is the alphabet review. There are no new letters today: you will practise all twenty eight letters, and finish with an exam on the whole alphabet.": "Wannan bitar baƙaƙe ce. Babu sabon harafi yau: za ka yi atisayen dukan baƙaƙe ashirin da takwas, ka gama da jarrabawa a kan dukan baƙaƙe.", "This is the big final check for sukun and tanween! Listen carefully and show what you know. You can try again as many times as you like.": "Wannan babbar jarrabawar ƙarshe ce ta sukun da tanwin! Saurara da kyau ka nuna abin da ka sani. Za ka iya sake gwadawa sau nawa kake so.", "This is the big final check for the madd letters! Listen carefully and show what you know. You can try again as many times as you like.": "Wannan babbar jarrabawar ƙarshe ce ta baƙaƙen madda! Saurara da kyau ka nuna abin da ka sani. Za ka iya sake gwadawa sau nawa kake so.", "This is the big final check for the shadda! Listen carefully and show what you know. You can try again as many times as you like.": "Wannan babbar jarrabawar ƙarshe ce ta shadda! Saurara da kyau ka nuna abin da ka sani. Za ka iya sake gwadawa sau nawa kake so.", "This is the big final check! Listen carefully, build the words, and show what you know. You can try again as many times as you like.": "Wannan babbar jarrabawar ƙarshe ce! Saurara da kyau, gina kalmomin, ka nuna abin da ka sani. Za ka iya sake gwadawa sau nawa kake so.", "This is the final exam of Beginner Four, and of the whole book Nour al-Bayan. Twenty questions on tajweed and spelling. You need ninety five percent to pass. Bismillah.": "Wannan jarrabawar ƙarshe ce ta Mafari 4, da ta dukan littafin Nour al-Bayan. Tambayoyi ashirin a kan tajwidi da rubutu. Kana buƙatar kashi casa'in da biyar don ka ci. Bismillah.", "This is the final exam of Beginner One. Twenty questions on every madd: alif, yaa and waw, big and small. You need ninety five percent to pass and move to Beginner Two.": "Wannan jarrabawar ƙarshe ce ta Mafari 1. Tambayoyi ashirin a kan kowace madda: alif, yaa da waw, babba da ƙarama. Kana buƙatar kashi casa'in da biyar don ka ci ka wuce zuwa Mafari 2.", "This is the final exam of Beginner Three: shadda, the sun laam, and everything before. Twenty questions. You need ninety five percent to pass and move to Beginner Four.": "Wannan jarrabawar ƙarshe ce ta Mafari 3: shadda, laamush shamsiyya, da duk abin da ya gabata. Tambayoyi ashirin. Kana buƙatar kashi casa'in da biyar don ka ci ka wuce zuwa Mafari 4.", "This is the final exam of Beginner Two: sukun, Hamzatul Wasl and tanween. Twenty questions. You need ninety five percent to pass and move to Beginner Three.": "Wannan jarrabawar ƙarshe ce ta Mafari 2: sukun, Hamzatul Wasl da tanwin. Tambayoyi ashirin. Kana buƙatar kashi casa'in da biyar don ka ci ka wuce zuwa Mafari 3.", "This is the final exam of the Preparatory level. Twenty questions: listening, reading, building and writing, from every lesson. You need ninety five percent to pass and move to Beginner One.": "Wannan jarrabawar ƙarshe ce ta matakin Share Fage. Tambayoyi ashirin: sauraro, karatu, gini da rubutu, daga kowane darasi. Kana buƙatar kashi casa'in da biyar don ka ci ka wuce zuwa Mafari 1.", "This is the very last check of the whole book! Listen carefully and show what you know. You can try again as many times as you like.": "Wannan ita ce jarrabawa ta ƙarshe ta dukan littafin! Saurara da kyau ka nuna abin da ka sani. Za ka iya sake gwadawa sau nawa kake so.", "This lesson covers the": "Wannan darasi ya ƙunshi", "Three dots above. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo uku a sama. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Three little teeth. No dots.": "Ƙananan haƙora uku. Babu ɗigo.", "Three more kinds of madd: the madd at a stop, the necessary madd of six counts, and the disjoined letters at the start of some surahs, like Alif Laam Meem.": "Ƙarin nau'ikan madda uku: maddar tsayawa, maddar lazim ta ƙidaya shida, da baƙaƙen muqatta'a a farkon wasu surori, kamar Alif Laam Mim.", "Three teeth, no dots. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Haƙora uku, babu ɗigo. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Three teeth, three dots. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Haƙora uku, ɗigo uku. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Three teeth: no dots, three dots above.": "Haƙora uku: babu ɗigo, ɗigo uku a sama.", "Today we will learn eight new letters, from Daal to Daad. Let's go!": "Yau za mu koyi sababbin baƙaƙe takwas, daga Daal zuwa Daad. Mu tafi!", "Today we will learn seven new letters, from Taa to Kaaf. Let's go!": "Yau za mu koyi sababbin baƙaƙe bakwai, daga Taa zuwa Kaaf. Mu tafi!", "Today we will learn the first seven letters, from Alif to Kha. Let's go!": "Yau za mu koyi baƙaƙe bakwai na farko, daga Alif zuwa Kha. Mu tafi!", "Today we will learn the last six letters, from Laam to Yaa. Then you will know the whole alphabet!": "Yau za mu koyi baƙaƙe shida na ƙarshe, daga Laam zuwa Yaa. Sannan za ka san dukan baƙaƙe!", "Today: Alif to Kha": "Yau: Alif zuwa Kha", "Today: Daal to Daad": "Yau: Daal zuwa Daad", "Today: Laam to Yaa": "Yau: Laam zuwa Yaa", "Today: Taa to Kaaf": "Yau: Taa zuwa Kaaf", "Trace the letter": "Zana harafin", "Two Passages": "Sassa Biyu", "Two Short Stories": "Gajerun Labarai Biyu", "Two dots above, deep bowl. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo biyu a sama, kwano mai zurfi. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Two dots above. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo biyu a sama. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Two dots below. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Ɗigo biyu a ƙasa. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Two more rules. Before baa, the noon becomes a hidden meem: that is iqlab. Before fifteen other letters it is half hidden with a nasal sound: that is ikhfa.": "Ƙarin dokoki biyu. Kafin baa, nun tana zama mim ɓoyayya: wannan shi ne iqlabi. Kafin wasu baƙaƙe goma sha biyar tana ɓoyuwa rabi da sautin hanci: wannan shi ne ikhfa'i.", "Two passages in everyday spelling: The Farmer, and the dua after the Adhan. Listen, repeat, then read alone.": "Sassa biyu a rubutun yau da kullum: Manomi, da addu'a bayan kiran sallah. Saurara, maimaita, sannan ka karanta kai kaɗai.", "Two passages: The Greatness of Allah, and The Blessings of Allah. Listen, repeat, then read alone.": "Sassa biyu: Girman Allah, da Ni'imomin Allah. Saurara, maimaita, sannan ka karanta kai kaɗai.", "Two short passages: The Muslim, and The Sparrow. Listen to each line, read it after the teacher, then read it alone.": "Gajerun sassa biyu: Musulmi, da Gwara. Saurari kowane layi, karanta shi bayan malami, sannan ka karanta shi kai kaɗai.", "Two short passages: The Qur'an, and The Day of Eid. Listen to each line, read it after the teacher, then read it alone.": "Gajerun sassa biyu: Alƙur'ani, da Ranar Sallah. Saurari kowane layi, karanta shi bayan malami, sannan ka karanta shi kai kaɗai.", "Two short stories: Sami and Yusuf, two good friends, and Aisha and Khadija, two neighbours. Listen to each line, read it after the teacher, then read it alone.": "Gajerun labarai biyu: Sami da Yusuf, abokai nagari biyu, da Aisha da Khadija, maƙwabta biyu. Saurari kowane layi, karanta shi bayan malami, sannan ka karanta shi kai kaɗai.", "Two short stories: Umar, and Karam. Listen to each line, read it after the teacher, then read it alone.": "Gajerun labarai biyu: Umar, da Karam. Saurari kowane layi, karanta shi bayan malami, sannan ka karanta shi kai kaɗai.", "Umar and Karam": "Umar da Karam", "Undo": "Soke", "Upright stroke with a dot. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Layi a tsaye mai ɗigo. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Upright stroke, no dot. The fatha is the small stroke above.": "Layi a tsaye, babu ɗigo. Fatha ita ce ƙaramin layi a saman harafi.", "Waw Madd: Everyday Spelling": "Maddar Waw: Rubutun Yau da Kullum", "Waw Madd: Short and Long": "Maddar Waw: Gajere da Dogo", "We start at the very beginning: the twenty eight letters of the Arabic alphabet, from Alif to Yaa.": "Za mu fara daga farko sosai: baƙaƙen Larabci ashirin da takwas, daga Alif zuwa Yaa.", "Welcome to Beginner Four, the rules of beautiful recitation. Today, four kinds of madd. Watch for the wavy maddah sign: it means a longer stretch.": "Barka da zuwa Mafari 4, dokokin kyakkyawan karatu. Yau, nau'ikan madda huɗu. Kula da alamar madda mai karkacewa: tana nufin ja mai tsawo.", "Welcome to Beginner Four: the rules of tajweed. First, four kinds of madd. Where you see the wavy maddah sign, stretch the vowel four to five counts.": "Barka da zuwa Mafari 4: dokokin tajwidi. Da farko, nau'ikan madda huɗu. Inda ka ga alamar madda mai karkacewa, ja wasalin ƙidaya huɗu zuwa biyar.", "Welcome to Beginner One: the madd letters. A madd makes a vowel long, for exactly two counts. We start with alif after fatha: ba becomes baa.": "Barka da zuwa Mafari 1: baƙaƙen madda. Madda tana tsawaita wasali, ƙidaya biyu daidai. Za mu fara da alif bayan fatha: ba ya zama baa.", "Welcome to Beginner Three. We start with a big review of everything so far: madd, sukun and tanween, in Qur'anic phrases.": "Barka da zuwa Mafari 3. Za mu fara da babbar bitar duk abin da aka koya: madda, sukun da tanwin, a cikin jimlolin Alƙur'ani.", "Welcome to Beginner Two. The sukun is a small circle above a letter. It means the letter has no vowel, so it closes the sound before it: a, then b, becomes ab.": "Barka da zuwa Mafari 2. Sukun ƙaramin da'ira ne a saman harafi. Yana nufin harafin ba shi da wasali, don haka yana rufe sautin da ke gabansa: a, sannan b, ya zama ab.", "Welcome to the alphabet review! You know all twenty eight letters. Listen, then pop the right balloon.": "Barka da zuwa bitar baƙaƙe! Ka san dukan baƙaƙe ashirin da takwas. Saurara, sannan ka fasa balan-balan da ya dace.", "Welcome to this level, the rules of beautiful recitation. Today, four kinds of madd. Watch for the wavy maddah sign: it means a longer stretch.": "Barka da zuwa wannan mataki, dokokin kyakkyawan karatu. Yau, nau'ikan madda huɗu. Kula da alamar madda mai karkacewa: tana nufin ja mai tsawo.", "Welcome to this level. The sukun is a small circle above a letter. It means the letter has no vowel, so it closes the sound before it: a, then b, becomes ab.": "Barka da zuwa wannan mataki. Sukun ƙaramin da'ira ne a saman harafi. Yana nufin harafin ba shi da wasali, don haka yana rufe sautin da ke gabansa: a, sannan b, ya zama ab.", "Welcome to this level. We start with a big review of everything so far: madd, sukun and tanween, in Qur'anic phrases.": "Barka da zuwa wannan mataki. Za mu fara da babbar bitar duk abin da aka koya: madda, sukun da tanwin, a cikin jimlolin Alƙur'ani.", "Welcome to this level: the madd letters. A madd makes a vowel long, for exactly two counts. We start with alif after fatha: ba becomes baa.": "Barka da zuwa wannan mataki: baƙaƙen madda. Madda tana tsawaita wasali, ƙidaya biyu daidai. Za mu fara da alif bayan fatha: ba ya zama baa.", "What is this letter called?": "Yaya ake kiran wannan harafi?", "What is this letter's name?": "Menene sunan wannan harafi?", "When two letters that are the same, or close, or from the same place meet, the first one merges into the second. Listen and read them as one doubled letter.": "Idan baƙaƙe biyu iri ɗaya, ko na kusa, ko daga wuri ɗaya suka haɗu, na farko yana shiga cikin na biyu. Saurara ka karanta su harafi ɗaya mai shadda.", "Where does the hamza sit in the middle of a word? On a yaa seat with kasra, on a waw with damma. Read each pair: one from the Mushaf, one in everyday spelling.": "Ina hamza take zama a tsakiyar kalma? A kan kujerar yaa idan da kasra, a kan waw idan da damma. Karanta kowane nau'i: ɗaya daga Mus'hafi, ɗaya a rubutun yau da kullum.", "Which letter does it start with?": "Da wane harafi yake farawa?", "Which letter has three teeth and no dots?": "Wane harafi ne yake da haƙora uku ba ɗigo?", "Which letter is hiding?": "Wane harafi ne yake ɓoye?", "Which letter is this (start of a word)?": "Wane harafi ne wannan (farkon kalma)?", "Which letter is this?": "Wane harafi ne wannan?", "Which letter makes a deep “q” from the back of the mouth?": "Wane harafi ne yake faɗin \"q\" mai zurfi daga bayan baki?", "Which letter makes “kh” as in loch?": "Wane harafi ne yake faɗin \"kh\"?", "Which letter?": "Wane harafi?", "Which one matches what you hear?": "Wanne ne ya dace da abin da ka ji?", "Which one?": "Wanne?", "Whole Words": "Cikakkun Kalmomi", "With the sun letters, the laam is written but not read. The next letter is doubled instead: ash shams, not al shams.": "Da baƙaƙen shamsiyya, ana rubuta laam amma ba a karanta ta. A maimakon haka, ana ninka harafin da ke biye: ash shams, ba al shams ba.", "Words and phrases in everyday spelling, with alif and yaa madd together. Read word by word, then the whole phrase.": "Kalmomi da jimloli a rubutun yau da kullum, da maddar alif da yaa tare. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya.", "Words and phrases with all three kinds of tanween. Look at the last letter, and read an, in, or un.": "Kalmomi da jimloli da dukan nau'ikan tanwin uku. Duba harafin ƙarshe, ka karanta an, in, ko un.", "Words and short sentences about the pillars of Islam, in everyday spelling. Read word by word, then the whole sentence.": "Kalmomi da gajerun jimloli game da rukunan Musulunci, a rubutun yau da kullum. Karanta kalma-kalma, sannan jimlar gaba ɗaya.", "Words in Two Steps": "Kalmomi a Matakai Biyu", "Words in everyday spelling with all three madd letters: alif, yaa and waw. Read each word in one go.": "Kalmomi a rubutun yau da kullum da dukan baƙaƙen madda uku: alif, yaa da waw. Karanta kowace kalma a lokaci ɗaya.", "Words with all three harakat. Read each letter, then join them, like shu, ri, ba: shuriba.": "Kalmomi da dukan harakoki uku. Karanta kowane harafi, sannan ka haɗa su, kamar shu, ri, ba: shuriba.", "Write": "Rubuta", "Write what you hear": "Rubuta abin da ka ji", "Writing": "Rubutu", "Writing time! Listen, then tap the letter you hear.": "Lokacin rubutu! Saurara, sannan ka danna harafin da ka ji.", "Yaa Madd: Everyday Spelling": "Maddar Yaa: Rubutun Yau da Kullum", "Yaa Madd: Qur'anic Words": "Maddar Yaa: Kalmomin Alƙur'ani", "You already know Alif to Daad!": "Ka riga ka san Alif zuwa Daad!", "You already know Alif to Kaaf!": "Ka riga ka san Alif zuwa Kaaf!", "You already know Alif to Kha!": "Ka riga ka san Alif zuwa Kha!", "You can read أَ – ذَ!": "Za ka iya karanta أَ – ذَ!", "You can read رَ – عَ!": "Za ka iya karanta رَ – عَ!", "You can read غَ – يَ!": "Za ka iya karanta غَ – يَ!", "You know the whole alphabet! أ – ي": "Ka san dukan baƙaƙe! أ – ي", "You know أ – خ!": "Ka san أ – خ!", "You know أ – ض!": "Ka san أ – ض!", "You know أ – ك!": "Ka san أ – ك!", "You know ا – ض. This lesson adds": "Ka san ا – ض. Wannan darasi yana ƙara", "You know ا – ك. This lesson adds the": "Ka san ا – ك. Wannan darasi yana ƙara", "You will hear a letter's name. Choose the letter.": "Za ka ji sunan harafi. Zaɓi harafin.", "Your turn — say it!": "Lokacinka, faɗe shi!", "Your turn! Listen to the letter, then tap the microphone and say its name.": "Lokacinka! Saurari harafin, sannan ka danna makirufo ka faɗi sunansa.", "Your turn! Listen, then tap the microphone and read it, like ba.": "Lokacinka! Saurara, sannan ka danna makirufo ka karanta, kamar ba.", "a breathy “h” from the throat": "\"h\" mai iska daga maƙogwaro", "a breathy “ḥa”": "\"ḥa\" mai iska", "a deep “qa”": "\"qa\" mai zurfi", "a deep “q” from the back of the mouth": "\"q\" mai zurfi daga bayan baki", "a dot (the shape of ص)": "ɗigo (siffar ص)", "a dot (the shape of ط)": "ɗigo (siffar ط)", "a dot above (the shape of ح)": "ɗigo a sama (siffar ح)", "a dot above (the shape of د)": "ɗigo a sama (siffar د)", "a dot above (the shape of ر)": "ɗigo a sama (siffar ر)", "a dot above (the shape of ع)": "ɗigo a sama (siffar ع)", "a gargled “gha”": "\"gha\" kamar kurkure", "a heavy “th” as in this": "\"dh\" mai nauyi", "a heavy “t”": "\"t\" mai nauyi", "a heavy “ḍa”": "\"ḍa\" mai nauyi", "a heavy “ṣa”": "\"ṣa\" mai nauyi", "a heavy, full “s”": "\"s\" mai nauyi kuma cikakke", "a letter. It adds a short “a”:": "harafi. Tana ƙara gajeren \"a\":", "a light “ha” (as in hat)": "\"ha\" mai sauƙi", "a light “h” as in hat": "\"h\" mai sauƙi", "a soft gargled “gh”": "\"gh\" mai laushi kamar kurkure", "a tapped “r”": "\"r\" mai bugawa", "and Qur'anic words": "da kalmomin Alƙur'ani", "b as in “book”.": "b kamar a \"baba\".", "d as in “door”, tongue tip touching behind the top teeth.": "d kamar a \"da\", kan harshe yana taɓa bayan haƙoran sama.", "f as in “fish”.": "f kamar a \"fata\".", "from the Mushaf": "daga Mus'hafi", "is read “ba”.": "ana karanta \"ba\".", "j as in “jam”.": "j kamar a \"jaki\".", "k as in “kite”.": "k kamar a \"kare\".", "kh as in Scottish “loch”, from the back of the mouth.": "kh daga bayan baki, kamar a \"khamis\".", "l as in “leaf”.": "l kamar a \"lafiya\".", "letter by letter, then joined": "harafi-harafi, sannan a haɗe", "m as in “moon”.": "m kamar a \"mota\".", "more Qur'anic phrases": "ƙarin jimlolin Alƙur'ani", "n as in “noon”.": "n kamar a \"nama\".", "review & shadda": "bita da shadda", "s as in “sun”.": "s kamar a \"sabo\".", "sh as in “ship”.": "sh kamar a \"shanu\".", "sukun & tanween": "sukun da tanwin", "t as in “tea”, tongue touching behind the top teeth.": "t kamar a \"tafi\", harshe yana taɓa bayan haƙoran sama.", "tajweed & spelling": "tajwidi da rubutu", "th as in “think”, tongue between the teeth. Never “s” or “z”.": "th, harshe tsakanin haƙora. Kada ka faɗi \"s\" ko \"z\".", "th as in “this”, tongue between the teeth. Never “z” or “d”.": "dh, harshe tsakanin haƙora. Kada ka faɗi \"z\" ko \"d\".", "the shape of د with a dot above": "siffar د da ɗigo a sama", "the shape of ر with a dot above": "siffar ر da ɗigo a sama", "the shape of ص with a dot above": "siffar ص da ɗigo a sama", "the shape of ط with a dot above": "siffar ط da ɗigo a sama", "the shape of ع with a dot above": "siffar ع da ɗigo a sama", "the special heavy “d” of Arabic": "\"d\" ta musamman mai nauyi ta Larabci", "the voiced squeeze from the throat (ʿayn)": "sauti mai murya da ake matsewa daga maƙogwaro (ʿayn)", "the whole book!": "dukan littafin!", "two letters, then the third": "baƙaƙe biyu, sannan na uku", "w as in “water”.": "w kamar a \"wasa\".", "y as in “yes”.": "y kamar a \"yaro\".", "z as in “zoo”.": "z kamar a \"zuma\".", "بَ says “ba”! Today: أَ – ذَ": "بَ ana karanta \"ba\"! Yau: أَ – ذَ", "بَ says “ba”! Today: رَ – عَ": "بَ ana karanta \"ba\"! Yau: رَ – عَ", "بَ says “ba”! Today: غَ – يَ": "بَ ana karanta \"ba\"! Yau: غَ – يَ", "رَ with fatha is read heavy (full mouth).": "رَ da fatha ana karanta ta da nauyi (baki a cike).", "ـًا  = an": "ـًا  = an", "ـٌ  = un": "ـٌ  = un", "ـٍ  = in": "ـٍ  = in", "ـُۥ in the Mushaf": "ـُۥ a Mus'hafi", "ـِۦ in the Mushaf": "ـِۦ a Mus'hafi", "ـٰ in the Mushaf": "ـٰ a Mus'hafi", "“a”: the letter + a short “a”. As in أَقْصَى (Al-Aqsa).": "\"a\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a أَقْصَى (Al-Aqsa).", "“ba”: the letter + a short “a”. As in بَيْت (house).": "\"ba\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a بَيْت (gida).", "“da”: the letter + a short “a”. As in دَائِرَة (circle).": "\"da\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a دَائِرَة (da'ira).", "“dha” (th as in this)": "\"dha\"", "“dha” (th as in this): the letter + a short “a”. As in ذَيْل (tail).": "\"dha\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a ذَيْل (wutsiya).", "“fa”: the letter + a short “a”. As in فَرَاشَة (butterfly).": "\"fa\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a فَرَاشَة (malam buɗe mana littafi).", "“gha” (soft gargled gh): the letter + a short “a”. As in غَسَّالَة (washing machine).": "\"gha\" (gh mai laushi): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a غَسَّالَة (injin wanki).", "“ha” (light h as in hat): the letter + a short “a”. As in هَرَم (pyramid).": "\"ha\" (h mai sauƙi): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a هَرَم (dala).", "“ja”: the letter + a short “a”. As in جَمَل (camel).": "\"ja\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a جَمَل (raƙumi).", "“j” as in jam": "\"j\" kamar a jaki", "“ka”: the letter + a short “a”. As in كَعْبَة (Kaʿbah).": "\"ka\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a كَعْبَة (Ka'aba).", "“kha” (as in loch)": "\"kha\"", "“kha” (kh as in loch): the letter + a short “a”. As in خَرُوف (sheep).": "\"kha\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a خَرُوف (rago).", "“kh” as in loch": "\"kh\"", "“k” as in kite": "\"k\" kamar a kare", "“la”: the letter + a short “a”. As in لَيْمُون (lemon).": "\"la\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a لَيْمُون (lemo).", "“ma”: the letter + a short “a”. As in مَوْز (bananas).": "\"ma\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a مَوْز (ayaba).", "“m” as in moon": "\"m\" kamar a mota", "“na”: the letter + a short “a”. As in نَخْلَة (palm tree).": "\"na\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a نَخْلَة (dabino).", "“qa” (deep q): the letter + a short “a”. As in قَلَم (pen).": "\"qa\" (q mai zurfi): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a قَلَم (alƙalami).", "“ra”: the letter + a short “a”. As in رَغِيف (loaf).": "\"ra\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a رَغِيف (burodi).", "“sa”: the letter + a short “a”. As in سَمَكَة (fish).": "\"sa\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a سَمَكَة (kifi).", "“sha”": "\"sha\"", "“sha”: the letter + a short “a”. As in شَمْعَة (candle).": "\"sha\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a شَمْعَة (kyandir).", "“sh” as in ship": "\"sh\" kamar a shanu", "“ta”: the letter + a short “a”. As in تَمْر (dates).": "\"ta\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a تَمْر (dabino).", "“tha” (th as in think)": "\"tha\"", "“tha” (th as in think): the letter + a short “a”. As in ثَلَّاجَة (fridge).": "\"tha\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a ثَلَّاجَة (firiji).", "“th” as in think": "\"th\"", "“th” as in this": "\"dh\"", "“wa”: the letter + a short “a”. As in وَرْدَة (rose).": "\"wa\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a وَرْدَة (fure).", "“w” as in water": "\"w\" kamar a wasa", "“ya”: the letter + a short “a”. As in يَد (hand).": "\"ya\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a يَد (hannu).", "“y” as in yes": "\"y\" kamar a yaro", "“za”: the letter + a short “a”. As in زَرَافَة (giraffe).": "\"za\": harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a زَرَافَة (raƙumin dawa).", "“z” as in zoo": "\"z\" kamar a zuma", "“ʿa” (the ʿayn from the throat): the letter + a short “a”. As in عَلَم (flag).": "\"ʿa\" (ʿayn daga maƙogwaro): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a عَلَم (tuta).", "“ʿa” from the throat": "\"ʿa\" daga maƙogwaro", "“ḍa” (heavy d): the letter + a short “a”. As in ضَابِط (officer).": "\"ḍa\" (d mai nauyi): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a ضَابِط (jami'i).", "“ḥa” (breathy h from the throat): the letter + a short “a”. As in حَمَامَة (dove).": "\"ḥa\" (h mai iska daga maƙogwaro): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a حَمَامَة (kurciya).", "“ṣa” (heavy s): the letter + a short “a”. As in صَارُوخ (rocket).": "\"ṣa\" (s mai nauyi): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a صَارُوخ (roka).", "“ṭa” (heavy t): the letter + a short “a”. As in طَائِرَة (plane).": "\"ṭa\" (t mai nauyi): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a طَائِرَة (jirgin sama).", "“ẓa” (heavy th): the letter + a short “a”. As in ظَرْف (envelope).": "\"ẓa\" (dh mai nauyi): harafi + gajeren \"a\". Kamar a ظَرْف (ambulan).", "↻ Start again": "↻ Sake farawa", "⌫ Delete": "⌫ Goge", "▶ My voice": "▶ Muryata", "▶ Play": "▶ Kunna", "▶ Spell": "▶ Rarraba", "▶ Start": "▶ Fara", "✔ Check": "✔ Duba", "🏅 Fatha Explorer": "🏅 Mai Binciken Fatha", "🏅 Letter Explorer": "🏅 Mai Binciken Baƙaƙe", "🏆 Alphabet Champion": "🏆 Gwarzon Baƙaƙe", "🐢 Slower": "🐢 A hankali", "👀 Show me": "👀 Nuna min", "💪 Heavy": "💪 Mai nauyi", "🔊 Hear it": "🔊 Ji shi", "🔊 Listen": "🔊 Saurara", "🔊 Play": "🔊 Kunna", "🔊 Whole phrase": "🔊 Jimlar gaba ɗaya", "🔊 Whole word": "🔊 Kalmar gaba ɗaya", "🧽 Clear": "🧽 Goge", "🪶 Light": "🪶 Mai sauƙi", "{0} · Lesson {1}": "{0} · Darasi {1}", "Level {0}": "Mataki {0}", "Beginner {0}": "Mafari {0}", "Lesson {0}": "Darasi {0}", "Lesson {0} exam": "Jarrabawar darasi {0}", "Step {0} of {1}": "Mataki {0} cikin {1}", "Question {0} / {1}": "Tambaya {0} / {1}", "{0} questions": "tambayoyi {0}", "{0} minutes": "minti {0}", "you need {0}% to pass": "kana buƙatar {0}% don ka ci", "you need every answer right ({0}%)": "dole ne duk amsoshi su zama daidai ({0}%)", "{0} questions ({1} review earlier lessons)": "tambayoyi {0} ({1} daga darussan baya)", "{0} letter": "harafi {0}", "{0} letters": "baƙaƙe {0}", "{0} missing": "{0} sun ɓace", "{0} more": "ƙarin {0}", "{0} letters with fatha": "baƙaƙe {0} da fatha", "All {0} letters": "Dukan baƙaƙe {0}", "all {0}": "duka {0}", "first {0}": "{0} na farko", "last {0}": "{0} na ƙarshe", "the last {0} letters!": "baƙaƙe {0} na ƙarshe!", "You know all {0} letters!": "Ka san dukan baƙaƙe {0}!", "{0} / {1} written correctly": "{0} / {1} an rubuta daidai", "{0} / {1} correct": "{0} / {1} daidai", "{0} / {1} heard correctly": "{0} / {1} an ji daidai", "{0} / {1} read correctly": "{0} / {1} an karanta daidai", "{0} of {1} correct": "{0} cikin {1} daidai", "{0} words read": "an karanta kalmomi {0}", "{0} phrases read": "an karanta jimloli {0}", "Part {0}": "Sashe {0}", "pp.{0}": "shafi {0}", "{0} Final Exam": "Jarrabawar Ƙarshe ta {0}", "Big Review {0}": "Babbar Bita {0}", "Madd Review {0}": "Bitar Madda {0}", "Hamza in the Middle {0}": "Hamza a Tsakiya {0}", "Noon Sakinah & Tanween {0}": "Nun Sakina da Tanwin {0}", "Review Practice {0}": "Atisayen Bita {0}", "Review: Verses & Hadith {0}": "Bita: Ayoyi da Hadisai {0}", "Shadda Phrases {0}": "Jimlolin Shadda {0}", "Sukun Phrases {0}": "Jimlolin Sukun {0}", "Sukun: Qur'anic Words {0}": "Sukun: Kalmomin Alƙur'ani {0}", "Types of Madd {0}": "Nau'ikan Madda {0}", "Same shape — {0}": "Siffa iri ɗaya: {0}", "It was {0}": "Amsar ita ce {0}", "That was {0}": "Wannan shi ne {0}", "Baa with a fatha says ba. Today we read {0} letters with fatha, from {1} to {2}. Listen and copy me!": "Baa da fatha ana karanta ta \"ba\". Yau za mu karanta baƙaƙe {0} da fatha, daga {1} zuwa {2}. Saurara ka kwaikwaye ni!", "In each lesson you learn, you say it out loud and the app checks you, you practise with short exercises, and you finish with an exam. You need {0} percent to pass, and you can retake it as many times as you like.": "A kowane darasi za ka koya, ka faɗa da ƙarfi manhajar ta duba ka, ka yi gajerun atisaye, ka gama da jarrabawa. Kana buƙatar kashi {0} don ka ci, kuma za ka iya sake ta sau nawa kake so.", "You will practise step by step, and finish with {0}. You need {1} percent to pass, and you can try again as many times as you like.": "Za ka yi atisaye mataki-mataki, ka gama da {0}. Kana buƙatar kashi {1} don ka ci, kuma za ka iya sake gwadawa sau nawa kake so.", "a final check": "jarrabawar ƙarshe", "an exam": "jarrabawa", "Listen, then write the {0} letters you hear.": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta baƙaƙe {0} da ka ji.", "Masha'Allah! You can read {0} letters with fatha! You earned the Fatha Explorer badge.": "Masha'Allah! Za ka iya karanta baƙaƙe {0} da fatha! Ka ci lambar Mai Binciken Fatha.", "This lesson: the first {0} letters with fatha:": "Wannan darasi: baƙaƙe {0} na farko da fatha:", "Today we learn {0} more: {1} to {2}!": "Yau za mu koyi ƙarin {0}: {1} zuwa {2}!", "Today we learn the first {0}: {1} to {2}!": "Yau za mu koyi {0} na farko: {1} zuwa {2}!", "Today: the last {0} letters, {1} to {2}!": "Yau: baƙaƙe {0} na ƙarshe, {1} zuwa {2}!", "You can read up to {0}. This lesson adds {1} more:": "Za ka iya karantawa har zuwa {0}. Wannan darasi yana ƙara {1}:", "You know the first {0}. This lesson adds": "Ka san {0} na farko. Wannan darasi yana ƙara", "is read “ba”. {0}": "ana karanta \"ba\". {0}", "(yaa). {0}": "(yaa). {0}", "{0} / {1} · {2}": "{0} / {1} · {2}", "Get them all right to win the badge · {0}": "Amsa duka daidai don ka ci lambar yabo · {0}", "Today you will meet {0} letters!": "Yau za ka haɗu da baƙaƙe {0}!", "Arabic has 28 letters, from Alif to Ya!": "Larabci yana da baƙaƙe 28, daga Alif zuwa Ya!", "Assalamu alaikum! I am Nuri. Arabic has 28 letters, from Alif to Ya.": "Assalamu alaikum! Ni ce Nuri. Larabci yana da baƙaƙe 28, daga Alif zuwa Ya.", "Same shape — only the dots change: 1 below, 2 above, 3 above.": "Siffa ɗaya, ɗigogi ne kawai ke canzawa: 1 a ƙasa, 2 a sama, 3 a sama.", "The course has five levels. Preparatory: the letters and the short vowels, called harakat. Beginner 1: madd, the long vowels. Beginner 2: sukun and tanween. Beginner 3: shadda. Beginner 4: the rules of tajweed, and Qur'anic spelling. Each level ends with a final exam and a certificate.": "Kwas ɗin yana da matakai biyar. Share Fage: baƙaƙe da gajerun wasula, wato harakoki. Mafari 1: madda, dogayen wasula. Mafari 2: sukun da tanwin. Mafari 3: shadda. Mafari 4: dokokin tajwidi da rubutun Alƙur'ani. Kowane mataki yana ƙarewa da jarrabawar ƙarshe da takardar shaida.", "alike in shape": "sun yi kama a siffa", "alike in sound": "sun yi kama a sauti", "Passed — lesson complete": "Ka ci, an gama darasi", "Not yet — practise and try again": "Tukuna: yi atisaye ka sake gwadawa", "Practise again": "Sake atisaye", "Retake": "Sake jarrabawa", "Try again": "Sake gwadawa", "✓ Back to lessons": "✓ Koma ga darussa", "Answer review": "Bitar amsoshi", "you:": "kai:", "answer:": "amsa:", "Masha'Allah · Barakallahu feekum": "Masha'Allah · Barakallahu feekum", "Microphone not available. Read it aloud, then continue.": "Babu makirufo. Karanta da ƙarfi, sannan ka ci gaba.", "Compare your voice with the teacher's:": "Kwatanta muryarka da ta malami:", "Not quite. Listen, then try again.": "Ba daidai ba tukuna. Saurara, sannan ka sake gwadawa.", "Listening… tap again to stop": "Ana sauraro… sake dannawa don tsayawa", "I read it correctly": "Na karanta daidai", "All built!": "An gina duka!", "Now let's test your ears!": "Yanzu mu gwada kunnuwanka!", "Same letter, same sound, different shapes": "Harafi ɗaya, sauti ɗaya, siffofi daban-daban", "Heavy: one of خ ص ض غ ط ق ظ": "Mai nauyi: ɗaya daga خ ص ض غ ط ق ظ", "Light": "Mai sauƙi", "alone": "shi kaɗai", "start": "farko", "middle": "tsakiya", "end": "ƙarshe", "madd": "madda", "shadda": "shadda", "fatha": "fatha", "kasra": "kasra", "damma": "damma", "sukun": "sukun", "fathatan": "fathatan", "kasratan": "kasratan", "dammatan": "dammatan", "Delete": "Goge", "Start again": "Sake farawa", "Continue ▶": "Ci gaba ▶", "Start the lesson": "Fara darasi", "Let's go": "Mu tafi", "questions": "tambayoyi", "A letter changes its shape at the start, the middle and the end of a word. But the sound stays the same!": "Siffar harafi tana canzawa a farko, tsakiya da ƙarshen kalma. Amma sautin ba ya canzawa!", "All matched": "An haɗa duka", "Almost! Listen and try again 👂": "Kusan! Saurara ka sake gwadawa 👂", "Back to lessons": "Koma ga darussa", "Build the word! Tap the pieces in order, starting from the right.": "Gina kalmar! Danna guntayen a jere, farawa daga dama.", "Clear": "Goge", "Compare your voice with the teacher's": "Kwatanta muryarka da ta malami", "Continue": "Ci gaba", "Continue where you stopped": "Ci gaba daga inda ka tsaya", "Did you say it like the teacher?": "Ka faɗe shi kamar malami?", "Done": "An gama", "Final check! You can do it.": "Jarrabawar ƙarshe! Za ka iya.", "Finish": "Gama", "From an earlier lesson": "Daga darasin baya", "From an earlier lesson: listen, then choose the letter.": "Daga darasin baya: saurara, sannan ka zaɓi harafin.", "I said it correctly": "Na faɗe shi daidai", "Let's read words! Each letter is read by itself, then together as one word. Read along with me.": "Mu karanta kalmomi! Ana karanta kowane harafi shi kaɗai, sannan tare a matsayin kalma ɗaya. Karanta tare da ni.", "Letter": "Harafi", "Level": "Mataki", "Lesson": "Darasi", "Question": "Tambaya", "Step": "Mataki", "Listen carefully, then tap the one you hear.": "Saurara da kyau, sannan ka danna abin da ka ji.", "Listen carefully, then tap the word you hear.": "Saurara da kyau, sannan ka danna kalmar da ka ji.", "Look at the shape. Which letter is it?": "Duba siffar. Wane harafi ne?", "Masha'Allah! Now it's your turn to play!": "Masha'Allah! Yanzu lokacinka ne ka yi wasa!", "Microphone not available — say it aloud, then continue.": "Babu makirufo: faɗe shi da ƙarfi, sannan ka ci gaba.", "My voice": "Muryata", "Next": "Gaba", "Next: the lesson exam.": "Na gaba: jarrabawar darasi.", "No microphone — just say it out loud 🙂": "Babu makirufo: kawai faɗe shi da ƙarfi 🙂", "Not quite. Listen again and repeat.": "Ba daidai ba tukuna. Sake saurara ka maimaita.", "Not yet — review and try again": "Tukuna: yi bita ka sake gwadawa", "Nour al-Bayan": "Nour al-Bayan", "Now write every letter you know, in order, starting from ا.": "Yanzu ka rubuta kowane harafi da ka sani a jere, farawa daga ا.", "Play": "Kunna", "Retake exam": "Sake jarrabawa", "Review the lesson": "Bita darasin", "Review": "Bita", "Show me": "Nuna min", "Some letters are heavy, and fill your mouth. Listen, and choose heavy or light.": "Wasu baƙaƙe masu nauyi ne kuma suna cika baki. Saurara, ka zaɓi mai nauyi ko mai sauƙi.", "Start": "Fara", "Tap the card to hear its name": "Danna katin don ka ji sunansa", "These letters look alike, or sound alike. Tap each one and listen carefully.": "Waɗannan baƙaƙe sun yi kama a siffa ko sauti. Danna kowane ka saurara da kyau.", "Try again!": "Sake gwadawa!", "Try the check again": "Sake jarrabawa", "We couldn't check automatically. Compare your voice with the teacher's": "Ba mu iya duba kai tsaye ba. Kwatanta muryarka da ta malami", "Well done!": "Madalla!", "Which letter is missing?": "Wane harafi ne ya ɓace?", "Write them in order": "Rubuta su a jere", "Writing time! Listen, then tap the letters you hear.": "Lokacin rubutu! Saurara, sannan ka danna baƙaƙen da ka ji.", "Yes 👍": "Ee 👍", "You need 95% — let's practise the ones you missed": "Kana buƙatar 95%: mu yi atisayen waɗanda ka rasa", "Your turn! Read the word, then tap the microphone and say it.": "Lokacinka! Karanta kalmar, sannan ka danna makirufo ka faɗe ta.", "letters and harakat": "baƙaƙe da harakoki", "sukun and tanween": "sukun da tanwin", "tajweed rules": "dokokin tajwidi", "madd, the long vowels": "madda, dogayen wasula", "<b>1. Madd Muttasil</b> (connected): a madd letter then a hamza <b>in the same word</b>: جَآءَ. Stretch <b>4–5 counts</b>.<br><b>2. Madd Munfasil</b> (separated): the madd letter ends one word and the hamza starts the next: إِذَآ أَصَٰبَتْهُم. <b>2 or 4–5 counts</b>.<br><b>3. Silah</b>: the small waw/yaa after هُ/هِ. <b>2 counts</b>, or <b>4–5</b> when a hamza follows (sign ٓ).<br><b>4. Badal & 'Iwad</b>: a hamza before the madd (ءَامَنُوا۟), or stopping on tanween fath (حَكِيمًا → hakeemaa). <b>2 counts</b>.": "<b>1. Madda Muttasil</b>: harafin madda da hamza ta biyo shi <b>a kalma ɗaya</b>: جَآءَ. Tsawo: <b>ƙidaya 4–5</b>.<br><b>2. Madda Munfasil</b>: harafin madda a ƙarshen kalma, hamza a farkon kalma ta gaba: إِذَآ أَصَٰبَتْهُم. <b>Ƙidaya 2 ko 4–5</b>.<br><b>3. Maddar Sila</b>: ƙaramar waw ko yaa bayan هُ ko هِ. <b>Ƙidaya 2</b>, ko <b>4–5</b> idan hamza ta biyo ta (alamar ٓ).<br><b>4. Maddar Badal da Maddar Iwad</b>: hamza kafin madda (ءَامَنُوا۟), ko tsayawa a kan tanwin fath (حَكِيمًا ← حَكِيمَا). <b>Ƙidaya 2</b>.", "<b>5. Madd 'Arid</b>: a madd letter before the last letter when you <b>stop</b> on it: نَسْتَعِينْ. <b>2, 4 or 6 counts</b>.<br><b>6. Madd Lazim</b>: a madd letter followed by a <b>shadda</b> (ٱلضَّآلِّينَ) or a fixed sukun (ءَآلْـَٰٔنَ). Always <b>6 counts</b>.<br><b>7. The disjoined letters</b> at the start of some surahs are read by their names: الٓمٓ = “Alif Laam Meem”. Letters marked ٓ get 6 counts; alif has no madd.": "<b>5. Madda Arid lis-Sukun</b>: harafin madda kafin harafin ƙarshe idan ka <b>tsaya</b> a wurin: نَسْتَعِينْ. <b>Ƙidaya 2, 4 ko 6</b>.<br><b>6. Maddar Lazim</b>: harafin madda da <b>shadda</b> ta biyo shi (ٱلضَّآلِّينَ) ko sukun na asali (ءَآلْـَٰٔنَ). Kullum <b>ƙidaya 6</b>.<br><b>7. Baƙaƙen muqatta'a</b> a farkon wasu surori ana karanta su da sunayensu: الٓمٓ = \"Alif Laam Mim\". Wanda ke da alamar ٓ ana jan shi ƙidaya 6; alif ba a jan ta.", "<b>Hamzatul Wasl</b> (ٱ) is the alif you only pronounce when you <b>start</b> with it. After a word it is silent: وَٱلْبَلَدِ is read “wal-balad”. With the <b>Qamariyyah laam</b> (ٱلْـ before letters like ب ج ح خ ع غ ف ق ك م و ه ي) you read the laam clearly: ٱلْقَمَرُ “al-qamar”.": "<b>Hamzatul Wasl</b> (ٱ) alif ce da ake furtawa kawai idan ka <b>fara</b> da ita; bayan kalmar da ke gabanta ba a karanta ta: وَٱلْبَلَدِ ana karanta \"wal-balad\". Da <b>laamul qamariyya</b> (ٱلْـ kafin baƙaƙe kamar ب ج ح خ ع غ ف ق ك م و ه ي), ana furta laam a fili: ٱلْقَمَرُ.", "<b>Ikhfa Shafawi</b>: meem sakinah before <b>ب</b>: close the lips lightly with ghunnah: هُم بِهِۦ.<br><b>Idgham Shafawi</b>: meem sakinah before <b>م</b>: merge them with ghunnah (2 counts): لَهُم مَّغْفِرَةٌ.<br><b>Izhar Shafawi</b>: before every other letter, a clear meem: أَنْعَمْتَ.<br><b>Noon and meem with shadda</b> always have <b>ghunnah of 2 counts</b>: إِنَّ, ثُمَّ.": "<b>Ikhfa'u Shafawi</b>: mim sakina kafin <b>ب</b>: rufe leɓuna a hankali da gunna: هُم بِهِۦ.<br><b>Idgamu Shafawi</b>: mim sakina kafin <b>م</b>: haɗa su da gunna (ƙidaya 2): لَهُم مَّغْفِرَةٌ.<br><b>Izharu Shafawi</b>: kafin sauran baƙaƙe, mim tana bayyana: أَنْعَمْتَ.<br><b>Nun da mim masu shadda</b> kullum suna da <b>gunna ta ƙidaya 2</b>: إِنَّ، ثُمَّ.", "<b>Iqlab</b>: before <b>ب</b> the noon turns into a hidden <b>meem</b> with ghunnah (marked with a small meem ۢ): مِنۢ بَعْدِ → “mim-ba'di”.<br><b>Ikhfa</b> (hiding): before the other 15 letters (ت ث ج د ذ ز س ش ص ض ط ظ ف ق ك) the noon is half-hidden, with ghunnah: كُنتُ.<br><b>Izhar Mutlaq</b>: noon sakinah then ي or و <b>in one word</b> stays clear: ٱلدُّنْيَا.<br><b>Tanween before Hamzatul Wasl</b> takes a kasra: خَيْرٌ ٱهْبِطُوا۟ → “khayrunih-bitoo”.": "<b>Iqlabi</b>: kafin <b>ب</b>, nun tana zama <b>mim</b> ɓoyayya da gunna (akwai ƙaramar mim ۢ): مِنۢ بَعْدِ ← \"mimba'di\".<br><b>Ikhfa'i</b>: kafin sauran baƙaƙe 15 (ت ث ج د ذ ز س ش ص ض ط ظ ف ق ك), nun tana ɓoyuwa rabi da gunna: كُنتُ.<br><b>Izhar Mutlaq</b>: nun sakina da ي ko و suka biyo ta <b>a kalma ɗaya</b> tana bayyana: ٱلدُّنْيَا.<br><b>Tanwin kafin Hamzatul Wasl</b> ana ba shi kasra: خَيْرٌ ٱهْبِطُوا۟ ← \"khayrunihbitu\".", "<b>Izhar</b> (clear): noon sakinah or tanween before a throat letter <b>ء ه ع ح غ خ</b>: read the noon clearly, no ghunnah: مَنْ ءَامَنَ.<br><b>Idgham with ghunnah</b>: before <b>ي ن م و</b> the noon merges into the next letter with a nasal sound of 2 counts: مَن يَقُولُ → “may-yaqool”.<br><b>Idgham without ghunnah</b>: before <b>ل ر</b> the noon disappears completely: مِن رَّحِمَ → “mir-rahim”.": "<b>Izhari</b>: nun sakina ko tanwin kafin baƙaƙen maƙogwaro <b>ء ه ع ح غ خ</b>: nun tana bayyana, babu gunna: مَنْ ءَامَنَ.<br><b>Idgami da gunna</b>: kafin <b>ي ن م و</b>, nun tana shiga harafin gaba da gunna ta ƙidaya 2: مَن يَقُولُ ← \"mayyaqulu\".<br><b>Idgami ba gunna</b>: kafin <b>ل ر</b>, nun tana ɓacewa gaba ɗaya: مِن رَّحِمَ ← \"mirrahima\".", "<b>Madd with alif.</b> When a letter with <b>fatha</b> is followed by a plain <b>alif</b> (ا), the “a” is stretched to <b>two counts</b>: بَ “ba” → بَا “baa”. Never longer than two counts, never shorter.": "<b>Madda da alif.</b> Idan harafi mai <b>fatha</b> <b>alif</b> (ا) ta biyo shi, ana jan sautin a <b>ƙidaya 2</b>: بَ ← بَا. Ba fiye ko ƙasa da 2 ba.", "<b>Madd with waw.</b> A letter with <b>damma</b> followed by a plain <b>waw</b> (و) is stretched to <b>two counts</b>: بُ “bu” → بُو “buu”.": "<b>Madda da waw.</b> Harafi mai <b>damma</b> da <b>waw</b> (و) ta biyo shi ana jan shi <b>ƙidaya 2</b>: بُ ← بُو.", "<b>Madd with yaa.</b> A letter with <b>kasra</b> followed by a plain <b>yaa</b> (ي) is stretched to <b>two counts</b>: بِ “bi” → بِي “bii”.": "<b>Madda da yaa.</b> Harafi mai <b>kasra</b> da <b>yaa</b> (ي) ta biyo shi ana jan shi <b>ƙidaya 2</b>: بِ ← بِي.", "<b>Mithlain</b> (identical): a letter with sukun then the <b>same</b> letter: they merge: ٱضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ.<br><b>Mutaqaribain</b> (close): letters close in sound and quality merge: بَل رَّبُّكُمْ → “bar-rabbukum”.<br><b>Mutajanisain</b> (same place, different quality) merge: قَد تَّبَيَّنَ → “qat-tabayyana”.": "<b>Mutamasilaini</b>: harafi mai sukun da <b>harafi iri ɗaya</b> ya biyo shi: ana haɗa su: ٱضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ.<br><b>Mutaqaribaini</b>: baƙaƙe biyu na kusa a makarji da sifa ana haɗa su: بَل رَّبُّكُمْ ← \"barrabbukum\".<br><b>Mutajanisaini</b> (makarji ɗaya, sifa daban) ana haɗa su: قَد تَّبَيَّنَ ← \"qattabayyana\".", "<b>Qalqalah</b>: ق ط ب ج د with sukun give a light echo.<br><b>Raa</b> is <b>light</b> with kasra, or sukun after kasra (رِزْقًا); <b>heavy</b> with fatha or damma (رَبَّنَا).<br><b>Small round zero ۟</b>: never read. <b>Oval zero ۠</b>: silent when you continue, read when you stop (أَنَا۠).<br>A madd letter before a sukun is dropped when you join: ذَاقَا ٱلشَّجَرَةَ → “dhaaqash-shajarah”.<br><b>Hamzatul Wasl</b> starts with <b>a</b> in ٱلْ, <b>u</b> when the 3rd letter has damma (ٱدْعُ), otherwise <b>i</b> (ٱضْرِبْ).": "<b>Qalqala</b>: ق ط ب ج د masu sukun suna ɗan yin amo.<br><b>Raa</b> tana <b>da sauƙi</b> da kasra, ko sukun bayan kasra (رِزْقًا); tana <b>da nauyi</b> da fatha ko damma (رَبَّنَا).<br><b>Ƙaramin sifiri zagaye ۟</b>: ba a taɓa karanta shi. <b>Sifiri mai tsawo ۠</b>: ba a karanta shi idan an haɗa, ana karanta shi idan an tsaya (أَنَا۠).<br>Harafin madda kafin mai sukun yana faɗuwa idan an haɗa: ذَاقَا ٱلشَّجَرَةَ ← \"dhaaqash-shajarata\".<br><b>Hamzatul Wasl</b> ana fara ta da <b>fatha</b> a ٱلْ, da <b>damma</b> idan harafi na uku yana da damma (ٱدْعُ), in ba haka ba da <b>kasra</b> (ٱضْرِبْ).", "<b>Shadda</b> (ـّ) means the letter is <b>doubled</b>: the first one has a sukun, the second one has the harakah. أَفْ + فُ = أَفُّ.": "<b>Shadda</b> (ـّ) tana nufin an <b>ninka</b> harafin: na farko yana da sukun, na biyu yana da wasali. أَفْ + فُ = أَفُّ.", "<b>Shadda</b> (ـّ) means the letter is <b>doubled</b>: the first one has a sukun, the second one has the harakah. بَدْ + دَ = بَدَّ.": "<b>Shadda</b> (ـّ) tana nufin an <b>ninka</b> harafin: na farko yana da sukun, na biyu yana da wasali. بَدْ + دَ = بَدَّ.", "<b>Shadda</b> (ـّ) means the letter is <b>doubled</b>: the first one has a sukun, the second one has the harakah. رَبْ + بِ = رَبِّ.": "<b>Shadda</b> (ـّ) tana nufin an <b>ninka</b> harafin: na farko yana da sukun, na biyu yana da wasali. رَبْ + بِ = رَبِّ.", "<b>Sukun</b> (ـْ) means <b>no vowel</b>: the letter is closed and joined to the letter before it. أَبْ is read “ab” in one beat, not “a-ba”. In the Mushaf the sukun looks like a small head of the letter haa.": "<b>Sukun</b> (ـْ) tana nufin <b>babu wasali</b>: harafin a rufe yake kuma yana haɗe da harafin da ke gabansa. أَبْ ana karanta \"ab\" a lokaci ɗaya, ba \"a-ba\" ba. A Mus'hafi sukun tana kama da ƙaramin kan ح.", "<b>Tanween Damm</b> (ـٌ) is a doubled harakah. It sounds like the harakah + a <b>noon sakinah</b>: بٌ = بُنْ “bun”. It comes only at the end of a word.": "<b>Tanwin damm</b> (ـٌ) wasali ne da aka ninka, sautinsa wasali + <b>nun sakina</b>: بٌ = بُنْ. Ana samun sa a ƙarshen kalma kawai.", "<b>Tanween Fath</b> (ـً) is a doubled harakah. It sounds like the harakah + a <b>noon sakinah</b>: بًا = بَنْ “ban”. It comes only at the end of a word.": "<b>Tanwin fath</b> (ـً) wasali ne da aka ninka, sautinsa wasali + <b>nun sakina</b>: بًا = بَنْ. Ana samun sa a ƙarshen kalma kawai.", "<b>Tanween Kasr</b> (ـٍ) is a doubled harakah. It sounds like the harakah + a <b>noon sakinah</b>: بٍ = بِنْ “bin”. It comes only at the end of a word.": "<b>Tanwin kasr</b> (ـٍ) wasali ne da aka ninka, sautinsa wasali + <b>nun sakina</b>: بٍ = بِنْ. Ana samun sa a ƙarshen kalma kawai.", "<b>The small alif</b> (ـٰ) appears only in the Mushaf. It is read exactly like a normal madd alif: <b>two counts</b>. هَٰذَا is read “haadhaa”. When it sits on a yaa or a waw (ىٰ ـوٰ), read the long “aa” and do <b>not</b> read the yaa or waw.": "<b>Ƙaramar alif</b> (ـٰ) tana cikin Mus'hafi kawai, kuma ana karanta ta daidai kamar maddar alif ta yau da kullum: <b>ƙidaya 2</b>. هَٰذَا ana karanta \"haadhaa\". Idan tana kan yaa ko waw (ىٰ ـوٰ), karanta maddar alif kuma <b>kada ka karanta</b> yaa ko waw.", "<b>The small waw</b> (ـۥ) appears only in the Mushaf, usually after هُ: لَهُۥ. It is read like a normal madd waw: “lahuu”, <b>two counts</b>.": "<b>Ƙaramar waw</b> (ـۥ) tana cikin Mus'hafi kawai, galibi bayan هُ: لَهُۥ. Ana karanta ta kamar maddar waw ta yau da kullum: \"lahuu\", <b>ƙidaya 2</b>.", "<b>The small yaa</b> (ـۦ) appears only in the Mushaf, usually after هِ: بِهِۦ. It is read like a normal madd yaa: “bihii”, <b>two counts</b>.": "<b>Ƙaramar yaa</b> (ـۦ) tana cikin Mus'hafi kawai, galibi bayan هِ: بِهِۦ. Ana karanta ta kamar maddar yaa ta yau da kullum: \"bihii\", <b>ƙidaya 2</b>.", "A letter can have a <b>shadda and a tanween</b> together: صَبٌّ “sabbun”, حَقًّا “haqqan”. Double the letter, then add the “n”.": "Harafi zai iya samun <b>shadda da tanwin</b> tare: صَبٌّ، حَقًّا. Ninka harafin, sannan ka ƙara n.", "An alif with a small round zero (ا۟) is <b>silent</b>: تُوبُوا۟ is read “tuubuu”. Do not read the alif.": "Alif mai ƙaramin sifiri zagaye (ا۟) <b>ba a karanta ta</b>: تُوبُوا۟ ana karanta \"tuubuu\". Kada ka karanta alif.", "An alif with a small round zero is <b>silent</b>, even in the middle of a word: مِا۟ئَةِ is read “mi-ah”.": "Alif mai ƙaramin sifiri zagaye <b>ba a karanta ta</b>, ko a tsakiyar kalma: مِا۟ئَةِ ana karanta \"mi-ah\".", "Hamza in the middle sits on an <b>alif</b> (أ) when it has fatha after a fatha or sukun; on the line (ء) after a madd or sukun letter. At the <b>end</b> of a word it follows the vowel before it: ئ after kasra, أ after fatha, ؤ after damma, and alone (ء) after a sukun or madd.": "Hamza a tsakiyar kalma ana rubuta ta a kan <b>alif</b> (أ) idan tana da fatha bayan fatha ko sukun, kuma a kan layi (ء) bayan harafin madda ko sukun. A <b>ƙarshen</b> kalma tana bin wasalin da ke gabanta: ئ bayan kasra, أ bayan fatha, ؤ bayan damma, kuma ita kaɗai (ء) bayan sukun ko madda.", "In everyday spelling a hamza in the middle sits on a <b>yaa seat</b> (ئ) when it has kasra or comes after a kasra: فِئَةٌ. It sits on a <b>waw</b> (ؤ) when it has damma or comes after a damma: يُؤْجَرُ. The Mushaf sometimes writes it differently.": "A rubutun yau da kullum, hamza ta tsakiya ana rubuta ta a kan <b>kujerar yaa</b> (ئ) idan tana da kasra ko kasra a gabanta: فِئَةٌ. Ana rubuta ta a kan <b>waw</b> (ؤ) idan tana da damma ko damma a gabanta: يُؤْجَرُ. Wani lokaci Mus'hafi yana rubuta ta daban.", "In everyday spelling the sukun is a small circle (ـْ). The alif of الْ has no mark at all: الْمَطَرُ.": "A rubutun yau da kullum, sukun ƙaramin da'ira ne (ـْ). Alif na الْ ba ta da alama: الْمَطَرُ.", "In words like هَٰذَا, ذَٰلِكَ, هَٰؤُلَآءِ, أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ and لَٰكِنَّ there is a long “aa” that is <b>read but not written</b>. The Mushaf shows it with a small alif (ـٰ); everyday spelling shows nothing: هَذَا is still read “haadhaa”.": "Kalmomi kamar هَٰذَا، ذَٰلِكَ، هَٰؤُلَآءِ، أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ، لَٰكِنَّ suna da dogon a da <b>ake karantawa amma ba a rubuta shi</b>. Mus'hafi yana nuna shi da ƙaramar alif (ـٰ); rubutun yau da kullum ba ya nuna komai: هَذَا ana karanta \"haadhaa\".", "The Mushaf (<b>Qur'anic spelling</b>) and normal books (<b>everyday spelling</b>) mark words differently: the sukun is a small head in the Mushaf but a circle in books; tanween can be stacked or staggered; Hamzatul Wasl is ٱ in the Mushaf but plain ا in books; ءَا in the Mushaf is آ in books; ىٰ in the Mushaf is ى in books.": "Mus'hafi (<b>rubutun Alƙur'ani</b>) da littattafai na yau da kullum (<b>rubutun yau da kullum</b>) sun bambanta a alamomi: sukun ƙaramin kai ne a Mus'hafi, da'ira kuma a littattafai; tanwin yana iya kasancewa a kan juna ko a jere; Hamzatul Wasl ٱ ta Mus'hafi alif ce ta yau da kullum ا a littattafai; ءَا ta Mus'hafi آ ce a littattafai; ىٰ ta Mus'hafi ى ce a littattafai.", "The letters <b>ق ط ب ج د</b> (qalqalah) bounce slightly when they have a sukun: يَخْطَفُ, أَدْبَرَ. Make a small echo, never a full vowel.": "Baƙaƙen <b>ق ط ب ج د</b> (qalqala) suna ɗan yin amo idan suna da sukun: يَخْطَفُ، أَدْبَرَ. Sa shi ɗan amo kaɗan, ba cikakken wasali ba.", "With the <b>sun letters</b> (ت ث د ذ ر ز س ش ص ض ط ظ ل ن) the laam of ٱلْ is <b>written but not read</b>, and the next letter takes a shadda: ٱلشَّمْسُ is read “ash-shams”.": "Da <b>baƙaƙen shamsiyya</b> (ت ث د ذ ر ز س ش ص ض ط ظ ل ن), ana <b>rubuta laam ta ٱلْ amma ba a karanta ta</b>, kuma ana ninka harafin da ke biye: ٱلشَّمْسُ ana karanta \"ash-shams\"."};
